{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792841840885-architect-dao-star-m1-reconcile-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md; cat docs/design/dao.stream.http.md; sed -n '30,108p' docs/design/dao.star.md\"","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-24 11:39:19 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-24 18:39:19 +0700\n\nI edited nothing. I read `memory_log.cljc`, `lease.cljc` (the medium declarations), `driver.cljc:330-350`, and the retention declaration in `dao/star/lease.cljc:217`. I did not read the codex findings file itself. Both rulings rest on your prompt's account of the findings.\n\n## Finding 3: the reviewer is right, and my prior claim was wrong\n\n`tick-subscriptions!` keeps a subscription in `:subs` until it sees `:lapsed` or `:gapped`. On http-kit no `:http/closed` is ever deposited. So the driver renews the exchange lease every tick, and the retained subscription renews the lineage lease too (`driver.cljc:343`). Neither lapses by silence. My sentence \"the responder's own control flow stops renewing for it\" described a stop that nothing performs, and the amended Sizing sentence (\"the duration is also the dead-peer detection bound\") has no support.\n\n### Ruling: (iii), a tenure cap. The lease's `:dao.lease/max` is the bound, and (ii) is the honest fallback for anything beyond it.\n\n**Why not (i), buffer exhaustion.**\n- It is an unverified hypothesis. Nobody has driven a write to exhaustion on http-kit.\n- Even if it holds, the bound is a function of socket buffer sizes, kernel settings and chunk size. That is not a number a composition can size against.\n- It would make the keep-alive chunk the detector, which is the conflation the spec's \"neither stands in for the other\" sentence exists to prevent.\n- It may be worth a later experiment, but a spec bound cannot rest on it.\n\n**Why a cap works where renewal does not.**\n- `dao.lease.md` says the cap bounds tenure from the first grant, and renewals do not move it. A holder that renews forever still reaches `at-bound?` and stops. That is the mechanism the lineage lease already uses (\"stops at its bound\").\n- Giving the *exchange* lease a `:dao.lease/max` bounds how long any one SSE exchange can stay open, whether or not its peer is alive. When the max is reached the driver stops renewing (`at-bound?`), the lease lapses, reclaim runs `close-exchange`, and the adapter deposits `:http/closed`. A live Datastar client sees the stream end and reconnects with `/s/<token>`, which is a new subscribe and a re-projection of the current occurrence. A dead peer is released.\n- Cost: every healthy subscription reconnects once per max. That is harmless, because subscribe consumes nothing and the projection is a derivation.\n- The bound is real, sized by the composition, and independent of the host's buffering behavior.\n\n**Check before relying on this.** I read the lease functions in `lease.cljc` only by name and docstring. `dao.star.md` says the lineage grant takes an optional `:dao.lease/max`, so the grant supports it. The implementer must confirm that `author-grant`/`grant` accepts `:dao.lease/max` for the *exchange* grant in the same way, and that the driver's exchange holders honor `at-bound?`. If they don't, the replacement text below overstates it. This is the one place I'm asserting something I haven't traced.\n\n**What stays unbounded.** A dead peer that holds an exchange *under its max* is still undetected until the max. Within the max there is no detection on a host that hides closure. That is the honest limit.\n\n### Replacement text\n\n**`dao.star.md`, Liveness, \"Keep-alive is the responder's\"** (replace the whole paragraph):\n\n> **Keep-alive is the responder's.** On its tick it may append an `:http/chunk` carrying an SSE comment line. That chunk is bytes for the wire, so a host that reports write failure discovers a dead peer by writing; the renewal is evidence for the judge. Neither stands in for the other. A peer's close or a reported write failure is deposited as `:http/closed`; the responder reads it as data and drops the exchange, and the judge ends the exchange lease with cause `:policy`. A host whose send buffers and whose close notification is silent for an idle exchange (http-kit is one) reports neither, so a chunk written to a dead peer is not evidence of anything, and a responder that keeps renewing a subscription it believes open keeps the lease alive. Such an exchange ends at its lease's `:dao.lease/max`, not before.\n\n**`dao.star.md`, Liveness, Sizing sentence** (replace the sentence \"A false lapse is possible\" paragraph's detection claim, and wherever the duration was named the detection bound):\n\n> The duration bounds silence, not death. The detection bound for a peer that disconnects while an exchange is idle is the exchange lease's `:dao.lease/max` on a host that does not report the close, and the host's own close notification, when it gives one, on a host that does. The composition sizes `:dao.lease/max` against the longest it will tolerate a dead subscription holding a socket and a driver slot, and accepts that every healthy subscription reconnects at that interval.\n\nThe exchange grant in Liveness should also say it carries `:dao.lease/max` (a duration), parallel to the lineage grant's optional cap. For exchanges, make it required for subscription exchanges, so that no subscription is uncapped.\n\n**`dao.stream.http.md`, Honest Limit** (replace the entry I proposed last time):\n\n> **A host may not report a peer that disconnects while an exchange is idle.** A host whose send buffers and whose close notification does not fire for an idle streaming exchange (http-kit, observed) gives the boundary no failed write and no close to deposit. The boundary invents none. The composition's lease is the detector, and for a responder that renews, only the lease's `:dao.lease/max` ends such an exchange. The boundary takes no clock and does not add one.\n\n### Honest test for the criterion\n\nTwo tests, as before, with the second corrected:\n1. Host-reported close deposits exactly one `:http/closed`.\n2. A silent subscription with a cap: the peer goes half-dead (the driver keeps renewing), the clock advances past the exchange lease's `:dao.lease/max`, and the test asserts that `close-exchange` ran, `:http/closed` was deposited and `:lapsed` was recorded. This replaces the \"lapses by `:silence`\" claim for subscriptions. The test must include a driver that renews on every tick, because that is the case the reviewer found.\n\nKeep the separate silent-exchange test for a non-renewing, never-answered exchange; that one still lapses by `:silence` as specified.\n\n**`jvm.clj`:** unchanged. The change is in the exchange grant (add the cap) and the specs.\n\n## Finding 4: confirmed. The session-facts medium must be complete history\n\n**Ruling:** reject my earlier ring-buffer ruling for session-facts. The spec says the medium is a complete-history transport and `dao.stream.md` says sizing cannot substitute for retention. Eviction would lose roots, and a lost root makes a live lineage unknown, which the router would answer as begin. That is a correctness failure, not a sizing one. Compaction stays deferred to OD-4.\n\n**Constructor:** `dao.stream.memory-log/create!` with the spec `{:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/memory-log}`. It must carry no `:dao.stream.memory-log/…` key, because that namespace is owned and empty, and a capacity key is rejected with `:dao.stream/invalid-spec`. Retention is complete by construction: the state is one vector dense from position 0, no expression removes an element, and `gap` is excluded.\n\n**Declaration to the lease constructors:** `make-judge`'s `:media` entry and the holder's `:fact` entry use `:medium {:retention :complete ...}` with no `:capacity`. `check-medium-declaration!` refuses a `:complete` medium that declares a capacity and an `:evict-oldest` one that declares none. Add `:value-domain` and `:attribution :envelope-key` as the existing declarations at `dao/star/lease.cljc:217` do for the evicting case. I only saw the `:retention :evict-oldest :capacity` line there, so the implementer should mirror the other keys from that helper.\n\n**Assembly requirement:** the driver and router constructors must refuse a session-facts medium whose declaration is not `:retention :complete`, throwing ex-info with `:refused :session-facts`, parallel to how the boundary refuses a reject-mode ingress. The check is on the declaration, not on handle introspection, which is the lease namespace's own rule.\n\n**Tests:** the Phase B tests create session-facts with `memory-log/create!` and declare it `:complete`. Add one test that the constructor refuses an `:evict-oldest` declaration, and one that drives past what the old ring-buffer capacity would have been and asserts the root fact is still readable from the origin.\n\n**Consequence worth noting:** with no `gap` possible on session-facts, the router and driver never take the gap path on that medium. Their gap handling for it becomes unreachable code, and the tests for it should use the lease medium or ingress instead. The lease medium is a separate question; I'd leave it evict-oldest, as the spec's Sizing paragraph treats it.\n\n**Not covered:** I did not check what else assumed a ring buffer in `dao/star/lease.cljc` beyond line 217, or how the two constructors share the declaration. The implementer should grep for `ringbuffer` and `:evict-oldest` under `src/cljc/dao/star/` and the tests.\n# DaoStream HTTP Boundary\n\nStatus: design, not implemented. Subordinate to\n[`dao.stream.md`](./dao.stream.md), which is the contract and wins on any\ndisagreement; sibling of [`dao.stream.ws.md`](./dao.stream.ws.md), whose\ndeposit model and admission rule it reuses. Every sentence below is a rule.\nThis document is application-agnostic: it specifies HTTP exchanges as\nevents and effects and nothing about what they carry.\n\n## What it is\n\nThe HTTP boundary is not a transport and owns no stream. It is an adapter\n(events in) and a host effect interpreter (effects out) over two ordinary\nmedia the composition supplies: an **ingress** medium it deposits into and\nan **egress** medium it reads. It has no reader surface, no `create!`, and\nhands no handle upward. It never reads a request body, a query string or a\nresponse chunk. Because nothing host-local crosses either medium, both are\n`:portable-values`, and the interpreter answering requests may sit on any\npeer (see *No privileged node*).\n\n## Exchange\n\nOne request and its response are one attachment; a connection is not\n(HTTP/1.1 keep-alive and HTTP/2 multiplexing are connection facts below\nthe transform). The boundary mints `:http/exchange` under the contract's\nserver-minted attachment rule (`dao.stream.md`, Envelopes): plain data,\nunique among the exchanges it can distinguish, and never reused for the\nlifetime of the egress medium. It carries the boundary's incarnation, so a\nstale effect retained from before a restart can never match a new socket.\n\n**Inventory.** The set of exchanges currently open is a resource the\nboundary possesses. It is not derivable from the ingress medium, which\nevicts. The boundary exposes it as one transport-owned operation beside\n`egress-step`, `open-exchanges`, answering the open ids, together with the\nidempotent `close-exchange`. Both exist for a `dao.lease.md` judge composed\ninside this boundary (reclaim procedure and restart inventory); code\nwritten against the contract may not reach for them.\n\n## Events in\n\nWire framing, header parsing and size limits happen below the transform;\nan over-limit or malformed request is answered there (400, 413, 503) and is\nnot an event. Every valid request is deposited unjudged. In these examples\nthe exchange id is `[incarnation n]` and strings stand for byte values:\n\n```clojure\n{:http/exchange [7 42]\n :http/event    :http/request\n :http/method   :post\n :http/path     \"/action\"\n :http/query    \"a=1\"\n :http/headers  {\"accept\" \"text/event-stream\"}\n :http/body     \"{\\\"count\\\":1}\"}\n\n{:http/exchange [7 42] :http/event :http/ended}\n{:http/exchange [7 42] :http/event :http/closed}\n```\n\n`:http/method` is a lower-case keyword; `:http/query` and `:http/body` are\nabsent when the request has none; header names are lower-cased.\n\nExactly one terminal event is deposited per exchange, after its request\nevent, whatever the cause: the peer closed, a write failed, an effect was\nout of order, the composition's judge reclaimed it, the boundary stopped.\n`:http/ended` is reserved for a response the boundary completed by\nperforming an `:http/end` effect. A terminal event reports that the\nexchange ended; it says nothing about which individual effects reached the\npeer.\n\n## Deposit admission\n\nAs `dao.stream.ws.md`, Deposit Admission. The constructor takes the\ningress destination and its admission declaration as data: evict-oldest\nretention with a declared capacity, value domain `:portable-values`, able\nto carry every envelope above, and a lifetime longer than the boundary.\nWiring a reject-mode destination is a host assembly defect refused at\nassembly. The constructor also takes `:http/max-open`, the number of\nexchanges held open at once, and `:http/max-body-bytes`; a request beyond\neither is answered below the transform and never deposited.\n\nEviction is loss. A reader whose cursor spans an ingress `gap` has missed\nrequest or terminal events and cannot reconstruct them from this medium;\nthe inventory above is where the possessing side's truth is.\n\n## Effects out\n\n`egress-step` is a step the composition drives at its own cadence, as it\ndrives `endpoint-step`. It holds one cursor on the egress medium, minted at\n`:dao.stream/newest` before the listener starts, and performs effects in\nthe egress medium's order:\n\n```clojure\n{:http/exchange [7 42] :http/effect :http/head\n :http/status 200 :http/headers {\"content-type\" \"text/plain\"}}\n{:http/exchange [7 42] :http/effect :http/chunk :http/body \"hello\"}\n{:http/exchange [7 42] :http/effect :http/end}\n```\n\n`:http/head` is sent once and first; `:http/chunk` writes bytes, a string\nas UTF-8, and flushes; `:http/end` completes the response and the\nexchange. The step appends no per-effect outcome, and a performed write is\nnot a delivery. A value that is not an effect for an exchange this boundary\nholds open is not this interpreter's and is ignored, whether it names\nnothing, names an exchange already ended or closed, or arrives after an\n`:http/end`: the egress medium has no privileged reader, and other\ninterpreters may share it. An effect out of order for an open exchange, a\nchunk before the head or a second head, closes that exchange.\n\nOrder is per medium. The ingress and egress media are two sequences, and\nno ordering holds between them; a writer that must know whether its effect\nwas performed asks a question the wire answers, by what the peer later\nsends, not this boundary.\n\nThe step takes no clock and holds no timer. How long a silent exchange is\nheld open is the composition's, through `dao.lease.md`; `close-exchange` is\nthe reclaim procedure a judge is composed with.\n\n## Observably gone\n\nA boundary that cannot deposit or cannot write makes itself observably\ngone by closing a resource it itself holds, the same action for every\ncause (`dao.stream.md`, Surfaces):\n\n- a non-`ok` ingress deposit closes that exchange's socket with no\n  synthesized response; the terminal event has nowhere to land, which is\n  the contract's irreducible corner;\n- a failed socket write closes the exchange and deposits `:http/closed`;\n- an egress `gap` closes every open exchange, since the step cannot say\n  whose effects were lost, then adopts the recovery cursor;\n- an egress `end` or `transport-error` closes every open exchange and the\n  listener: the boundary can never answer again.\n\nIt invokes nothing above itself, retries nothing, and interprets nothing.\n\n**A host may not report a peer that disconnects while an exchange is idle.** A host whose send buffers and whose close notification does not fire for an idle streaming exchange (http-kit, observed) gives the boundary no failed write and no close to deposit. The boundary invents none. The composition's lease is the detector, and for a responder that renews, only the lease's `:dao.lease/max` ends such an exchange. The boundary takes no clock and does not add one (architect ruling 2026-10-24, `collab/1792841840885-architect-dao-star-m1-reconcile-r2`).\n\n## No privileged node\n\nWhich end accepted is an establishment fact: HTTP has a requester and a\nresponder because TCP has a dialer and an acceptor, and a browser can only\ndial (`dao.stream.remote.md`, section 1). The ingress and egress media are\nordinary streams, so a peer that cannot listen may run the answering\ninterpreter against reflections of them served by a reachable peer that\nruns only this boundary. The boundary records no role beyond the exchange.\n\nHosts: clj (http-kit is already a dependency of the WebSocket transport),\ncljs on Node, cljd. A browser has no listener.\n\n## Deferred\n\n- An HTTP channel for `dao.stream.remote.md` (request maps by POST, answers\n  by a long-lived response) for peers that cannot open a WebSocket.\n- Request bodies as streams rather than one bounded value.\n- TLS termination, CORS and compression: below the transform, unspecified\n  here.\n\n1. **Events In**: A user clicks a button (`data-on-click=\"@post('/k/<token>')\"`). Datastar fires a standard HTTP request. The generic HTTP boundary (`dao.stream.http.md`) mints an exchange id, deposits the request as an unjudged `:http/request` event into the ingress `dao.stream` the composition wired, and holds the socket open. It reads nothing inside the request.\n2. **Routing**: A router step in the `dao.star` composition reads the ingress with its own cursor, classifies each request by its path (*Sessions and request kinds*), and forwards it to the medium of the session its token names, together with every later terminal event of that exchange. The boundary does not route.\n3. **Resuming**: The session's driver, on its next poll, observes the input at its own cursor and steps the parked continuation. Nothing wakes anything; a stream invokes nothing.\n4. **Semantics and State**: The `yin.vm` agent evaluates business logic linearly. The UI is a derivation of the continuation's state, never stored: the agent projects it into Datastar's SSE wire format (`event: datastar-patch-elements\\ndata: <div>...</div>`) through one pure projection function the composition supplies.\n5. **Effects Out**: The agent appends to the egress `dao.stream`, tagged with the exchange id: an `:http/head` effect (status, `Content-Type: text/event-stream`), one `:http/chunk` per SSE event with the fully constructed string, and `:http/end` when the response is complete. A subscription exchange simply never ends.\n6. **Dumb Socket Routing**: The boundary's `egress-step` observes the egress stream, matches the exchange id to the open socket, and flushes the unmodified payload. Datastar morphs the DOM. The agent parks again, waiting for the next input, for as long as it takes.\n\n### Sessions and request kinds\n\nA **lineage** is one session's chain of occurrences: a root and every successor a consumed input produced. **The token is the occurrence id**, minted unguessable by the driver; the lineage's identity is its root's id. Every projected UI carries the id of the occurrence that rendered it. The lineage's **current** occurrence is the one with no successor.\n\nThe driver appends one fact per transition to the **session-facts** medium, and appends it with `:dao.stream/ok` before any UI carrying the new id is projected:\n\n```clojure\n{:dao.star/lineage S :dao.star/occurrence S}                            ; root\n{:dao.star/lineage S :dao.star/occurrence O2 :dao.star/predecessor O1}  ; consumption\n{:dao.star/lineage S :dao.star/ended :halted}                           ; the program finished\n```\n\nThe router materializes occurrence → lineage → current from these facts and from the lease medium's `:lapsed` records (*Liveness*), as `dao.space.index` materializes a covered index, never from a table it keeps. The session-facts medium is a complete-history transport (`dao.stream.md`, Complete history); its growth is bounded only by OD-4's resolution, an open dependency.\n\n**Observation order.** A fact's `ok` is publication, not the router's observation of it, so the router never classifies from a projection that may lag. Each router pass reads the ingress first, then drains its session-facts and lineage-lease cursors to `blocked`, then classifies what it read. A token reaches the ingress only through a UI projected after its fact was accepted, so a fact precedes every request that names it, and a pass that has read the request has the fact to drain. The same holds for successor ids.\n\nThe drain proves this only on a direct handle: a reflection answers `blocked` while its request to the source is pending (`dao.stream.remote.md`, 2.4), which says nothing about the source. So **the router is composed on the peer that holds the session-facts medium, the lineage judge and the drivers**, and reads those two classification media directly; any other medium may be a reflection, which is the topology *Roles, not nodes* permits, so a driver separated from the HTTP boundary observes exchange grants and lapses over a reflection of the boundary's lease medium. A reflected ingress delays the read of a request, never its fact, so the proof stands. A router that read its facts through a reflection could not classify unknown at all; that composition is not permitted.\n\nThe router classifies by path; the boundary reads neither path nor token.\n\n| Path | Kind | What it does |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/` (no token) | begin | The root program starts a fresh lineage and answers a complete `text/html` document: `datastar.js`, actions carrying the root id, and `data-init=\"@get('/s/<token>')\"`. |\n| `/s/<token>` | subscribe | Opens the session's long-lived SSE exchange. Consumes nothing and advances nothing: the driver answers the head and a projection of the current occurrence, and every later patch goes here too. Reconnecting with the original URL is a new subscribe, resolved to the current occurrence however many inputs have passed. |\n| `/k/<token>`, token current | input | Consumed by the current occurrence (*Inputs, order and replay*). |\n| `/k/<token>`, token consumed | stale | Runs nothing. Answered by a projection of the current occurrence, then `:http/end`. |\n| any token of an ended or unknown lineage | begin | Halted, lapsed, or lost to a restart: answered as `/`. Unknown is judged only after the drain above. |\n\nSubscribe and stale requests are **re-projections**: the driver applies the projection function to the parked state without stepping it.\n\n### Signals\n\nA Datastar request carries the client's signals: in the `datastar` query parameter for GET and DELETE, in the JSON body otherwise. The boundary deposits them where HTTP put them, inside `:http/query` or `:http/body`, unread.\n\nDecoding is interpretation. `dao.star` supplies one pure projection from a request event to a signals map. The ingress tuple gains no slot for it, and signals become datoms only when an application interpreter derives them from the retained ingress stream (`datom.world.md`, Derive, don't persist).\n\nSignals are client-held state that moves, not shared state: each request carries an immutable snapshot, and the agent changes them only by appending a `datastar-patch-signals` effect. They are also the client's unverified claim. A signal is input to a continuation, never its state and never authority.\n\n### Inputs, order and replay\n\n**The token is the gate.** It is the request's only routing and idempotence key, and until ShiBi is load-bearing it is the sole gate on Mode 1 input: a pre-shared value in `dao.shibi.md`'s sense (owner ruling 2026-10-07).\n\n**Order is the ingress position.** Two inputs for one occurrence are not concurrent once deposited: one is earlier. Custody decides who consumes it. In a one-process composition the session's single driver is the only resumer; that exclusion is process-scoped and says so. Where more than one peer observes the ingress, resumption is a take, and a take is a lease on the occurrence (UCF §7.7).\n\n**One input, one successor.** Consuming an input advances occurrence `O` to its successor `O'` and appends the lineage fact. The reply goes to the exchange that carried the consumed input; patches for the session go to its open subscription exchanges, which the driver holds as its own interpreter state, built from the subscribe requests and terminal events routed to it.\n\n**Stale input is one-shot** (owner ruling 2026-10-07). A double click, a retry, a replayed URL, a second tab or the back button names an `O` that already has a successor. It runs nothing and is re-projected. The UI is a derivation, so answering twice is harmless, and a retry whose first reply was lost still converges. Mode 1 continuations are one-shot; multi-shot forks are deferred.\n\n**Effects.** Exactly-once needs a fenced writer into an enrolled consumer (UCF §7.7.5). Every other stream is at-least-once and declared so.\n\n### Liveness\n\nTwo leased resources, kept apart. Neither adds a clock to the wait for input: a parked continuation's `next` on its input is `blocked` until a request arrives, on a Tuesday or a Thursday.\n\n**The open exchange is leased.** The judge runs inside the peer that holds the HTTP boundary and is composed with the boundary's `close-exchange` as reclaim procedure and `open-exchanges` as its inventory (`dao.stream.http.md`, Inventory). For each `:http/request` it observes it grants unsolicited on a lease medium it writes: subject `{:http/exchange x}`, holder the egress medium's identity, a duration in `{:ms 1 :s 1000}`, and a `:dao.lease/max` cap that subscription exchanges are required to carry, so no subscription is uncapped (architect ruling 2026-10-24, `collab/1792841840885-architect-dao-star-m1-reconcile-r2`). Reclaim closes the exchange; the adapter deposits `:http/closed`, then the judge records `:lapsed`. A responder that keeps an exchange open observes its grant and appends `{:dao.lease/event :dao.lease/renewal :dao.lease/lease L}` to the egress medium at under half the duration, from its own control flow, against its own tick stream. The judge and `egress-step` are peer observers of that medium; each ignores the other's facts. A one-shot responder answers inside the granted duration and renews nothing. An exchange nobody answers lapses by `:silence`; Datastar's reconnect opens a new one.\n\n**A gap is loss, and nothing is forwarded about it.** The judge, on an ingress `gap`, reconciles both ways against the inventory: an open exchange without a lease is granted afresh, and a leased exchange absent from the inventory is recorded `:lapsed` with cause `:policy`, so nothing is held unleased and nothing closed stays leased (inventory reconciliation; `dao.lease.md`'s reclaim-and-regrant is reserved for a lost ledger). The router forwards nothing about a gap: a request or terminal event lost in the evicted window is unrouted, and a forward whose `append!` answers anything but `ok` is the same loss; an unrouted request's exchange lapses by `:silence`. Drivers learn that an exchange is gone from the lease medium they already read for their grants: a `:lapsed` record for one of their exchanges drops it (`dao.lease.md`, Carriage). A driver whose cursor on any medium it reads answers `gap` forgets every subscription it holds and renews none; they lapse by `:silence` and close, and Datastar's reconnect subscribes again. Session media are declared at assembly like any deposit destination, evict-oldest with a capacity, and sized against the driver's lag.\n\n**Keep-alive is the responder's.** On its tick it may append an `:http/chunk` carrying an SSE comment line. That chunk is bytes for the wire, so a host that reports write failure discovers a dead peer by writing; the renewal is evidence for the judge. Neither stands in for the other. A peer's close or a reported write failure is deposited as `:http/closed`; the responder reads it as data and drops the exchange, and the judge ends the exchange lease with cause `:policy`. A host whose send buffers and whose close notification is silent for an idle exchange (http-kit is one) reports neither, so a chunk written to a dead peer is not evidence of anything, and a responder that keeps renewing a subscription it believes open keeps the lease alive. Such an exchange ends at its lease's `:dao.lease/max`, not before (architect ruling 2026-10-24, `collab/1792841840885-architect-dao-star-m1-reconcile-r2`).\n\n**The lineage is leased** (owner ruling 2026-10-07; the holder choice below is the architect's). A lineage nobody returns to is reclaimed through `dao.lease.md`, not by a timer. The peer holding the parked record is the grantor. When a lineage begins, its judge grants unsolicited on the lease medium: subject and holder `{:dao.star/lineage S}`, duration the composition's idle allowance, `:dao.lease/max` optional. Attribution is by envelope key: the session-facts medium is written only by session drivers, each stamping `:dao.star/lineage` on its facts, renewals and release, and the judge's resolver reads that key; until ShiBi, any writer of that medium can renew, the same exposure the exchange lease has. The driver observes its grant before consuming or projecting, renews at under half the duration from its own control flow, on each consumed input and on its tick while it holds an open subscription, and **stops at its bound**: past it, it consumes nothing and projects nothing, and an input arriving then is handed to the root program as begin. So a connected session is retained for as long as it stays connected, by design, bounded only by the cap; a disconnected one lapses after the idle allowance. The lease ends with the lineage: released by the driver on halt, lapsed by the judge on silence. Reclaim retires the runnable resource, the current parked record; the `:lapsed` record on the lease medium is the judge's own and is what ends the lineage for the router. History, successor facts and lease records are kept (`dao.lease.md`: a reclaim frees the resource, never the record). The subject is distinct from Mode 2's custody subject `{:yin.k/occurrence O}` on the arbitration medium. Leases are process-scoped until the composition settles the three durable duties `dao.lease.md` names.\n\nSizing: duration exceeds twice the renewal interval; the keep-alive interval stays under the shortest proxy or NAT idle timeout on the path; the ingress window exceeds router and judge lag and each session medium's window exceeds its driver's; a boundary restart loses sockets and ledger together, so its exchange inventory to reclaim is empty. The duration bounds silence, not death. The detection bound for a peer that disconnects while an exchange is idle is the exchange lease's `:dao.lease/max` on a host that does not report the close, and the host's own close notification, when it gives one, on a host that does. The composition sizes `:dao.lease/max` against the longest it will tolerate a dead subscription holding a socket and a driver slot, and accepts that every healthy subscription reconnects at that interval. A false lapse is possible (`dao.lease.md`, Limits).\n\n---\n\n## Mode 2: The Fat Client (Mobile Continuations via UCF)\n\nStatus: proposed. Everything in this section waits on UCF version 1, fenced custody with a `dao.space` transactor as arbitration authority (`yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` §7.7, 7.7.8). Version 0 is fork-only and cannot offer the exclusivity below.\n\nWhile `dao.star` champions the dumb terminal, it is not locked into it. Because `yin.vm` continuations are pure data, they can cross the network boundary to act as SPA-style fat clients for low-latency local interaction.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/lease.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/router.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/signals.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.star.lease\n     2\t  \"The dao.lease compositions of dao.star Mode 1 (docs/design/dao.star.md,\n     3\t   Liveness): the stream-reading helper, the holder agent a driver threads per\n     4\t   lease, and the two grantor-side wrappers (exchange lease, lineage lease)\n     5\t   that author grants and drive the judge.\n     6\t\n     7\t   Nothing here reads a clock.  Time is the `:dao.lease/reading` data drained\n     8\t   from a tick stream the composition feeds, so every lapse is driven by\n     9\t   appending a tick.\"\n    10\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n    11\t            [dao.lease :as lease]\n    12\t            [dao.star.facts :as facts]\n    13\t            [dao.stream :as stream]))\n    14\t\n    15\t\n    16\t(defn- ok?\n    17\t  [r]\n    18\t  (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\t(defn oldest-cursor\n    22\t  [handle]\n    23\t  (let [r (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-oldest)]\n    24\t    (when-not (ok? r)\n    25\t      (throw (ex-info \"cannot mint a cursor\" {:outcome r})))\n    26\t    (:dao.stream/cursor r)))\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\t(defn drain\n    30\t  \"Read `handle` from `cursor` to `blocked`, never waiting.  Answers\n    31\t   `{:cursor c :values [v...] :gap? bool :end? bool}`: a `gap` is noted and\n    32\t   reading continues from its recovery cursor, as the contract has it.\"\n    33\t  [handle cursor]\n    34\t  (loop [c cursor values [] gap? false]\n    35\t    (let [r (stream/next handle c)]\n    36\t      (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n    37\t        :dao.stream/ok (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj values (:dao.stream/value r)) gap?)\n    38\t        :dao.stream/gap (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) values true)\n    39\t        :dao.stream/end {:cursor c :values values :gap? gap? :end? true}\n    40\t        {:cursor c :values values :gap? gap? :end? false}))))\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    44\t;; Holder agent: one lease, held by a driver's control flow\n    45\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    46\t\n    47\t(defn make-agent\n    48\t  \"A holder over `lease/make-holder` plus the cursors its control flow drains.\n    49\t   `config` is `make-holder`'s, less the cursors (minted here at the oldest\n    50\t   anchor, so a grant already on the medium is observed).  `:envelope` is merged\n    51\t   into every fact the agent appends (the lineage lease stamps\n    52\t   `:dao.star/lineage` here, which is what the judge's resolver attributes by).\n    53\t   Answers an atom holding the agent state.\"\n    54\t  [{:keys [tick fact writer envelope] :as config}]\n    55\t  (let [wired (lease/make-holder\n    56\t                (assoc config\n    57\t                       :tick {:handle tick :cursor (oldest-cursor tick)}\n    58\t                       :fact {:handle (:handle fact)\n    59\t                              :cursor (oldest-cursor (:handle fact))\n    60\t                              :source (:source fact)\n    61\t                              :medium (:medium fact)}\n    62\t                       :writer writer))]\n    63\t    (atom {:holder (:holder wired)\n    64\t           :tick (:tick wired)\n    65\t           :fact (:fact wired)\n    66\t           :writer (:writer wired)\n    67\t           :envelope (or envelope {})\n    68\t           :reading nil\n    69\t           :lapsed? false\n    70\t           :gapped? false\n    71\t           :release nil})))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t(defn- lease-id\n    75\t  [a]\n    76\t  (get-in a [:holder :grant :dao.lease/lease]))\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\t(defn step!\n    80\t  \"One control-flow pass of the holder: drain its own tick cursor for the\n    81\t   newest reading, then observe its grant (before anything else) and any\n    82\t   `:lapsed` record for its lease.  The fact cursor is read only once a reading\n    83\t   exists: a grant published before the holder's first tick stays unread on the\n    84\t   medium until a reading can observe it.  A `gap` on either cursor marks the\n    85\t   agent `:gapped?`: it renews nothing from then on.  Answers the new state.\"\n    86\t  [agent]\n    87\t  (swap!\n    88\t    agent\n    89\t    (fn [a]\n    90\t      (let [t (drain (get-in a [:tick :handle]) (get-in a [:tick :cursor]))\n    91\t            reading (or (some-> (filter #(= :dao.lease/tick (:dao.lease/event %))\n    92\t                                        (:values t))\n    93\t                                last\n    94\t                                :dao.lease/reading)\n    95\t                        (:reading a))\n    96\t            a (-> a\n    97\t                  (assoc :reading reading)\n    98\t                  (assoc-in [:tick :cursor] (:cursor t))\n    99\t                  (update :gapped? #(or % (:gap? t))))]\n   100\t        (if (nil? reading)\n   101\t          a\n   102\t          (let [f (drain (get-in a [:fact :handle]) (get-in a [:fact :cursor]))\n   103\t                a (-> a\n   104\t                      (assoc-in [:fact :cursor] (:cursor f))\n   105\t                      (update :gapped? #(or % (:gap? f))))]\n   106\t            (reduce\n   107\t              (fn [a v]\n   108\t                (cond\n   109\t                  (nil? (get-in a [:holder :grant]))\n   110\t                  (update a :holder lease/observe-grant (get-in a [:fact :source]) v reading)\n   111\t\n   112\t                  (and (= :dao.lease/lapsed (:dao.lease/status v))\n   113\t                       (some? (lease-id a))\n   114\t                       (= (lease-id a) (:dao.lease/lease v)))\n   115\t                  (assoc a :lapsed? true)\n   116\t\n   117\t                  :else a))\n   118\t              a\n   119\t              (:values f))))))))\n   120\t\n   121\t\n   122\t(defn gapped?\n   123\t  \"True once any cursor the agent reads answered `gap`.\"\n   124\t  [agent]\n   125\t  (boolean (:gapped? @agent)))\n   126\t\n   127\t\n   128\t(defn release-pending?\n   129\t  \"True while a release fact is staged and not yet appended with `ok`.\"\n   130\t  [agent]\n   131\t  (some? (:release @agent)))\n   132\t\n   133\t\n   134\t(defn holding?\n   135\t  \"May the control flow act: a grant observed, not stopped, not at its bound,\n   136\t   not lapsed, and no gap seen.\"\n   137\t  [agent]\n   138\t  (let [a @agent]\n   139\t    (boolean (and (not (:lapsed? a))\n   140\t                  (not (:gapped? a))\n   141\t                  (some? (:reading a))\n   142\t                  (lease/holding? (:holder a) (:reading a))))))\n   143\t\n   144\t\n   145\t(defn granted?\n   146\t  [agent]\n   147\t  (some? (get-in @agent [:holder :grant])))\n   148\t\n   149\t\n   150\t(defn past-bound?\n   151\t  \"True once the agent has left the lease for good: it lapsed, was released,\n   152\t   or reached its bound.  A gap is not that: the agent renews nothing after one\n   153\t   but the lease is not known to be over.\"\n   154\t  [agent]\n   155\t  (let [a @agent]\n   156\t    (boolean (or (:lapsed? a)\n   157\t                 (get-in a [:holder :released?])\n   158\t                 (get-in a [:holder :bound-reached?])\n   159\t                 (and (some? (:reading a)) (some? (get-in a [:holder :grant]))\n   160\t                      (lease/at-bound? (:holder a) (:reading a)))))))\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t(defn- append-renewal!\n   164\t  [agent]\n   165\t  (let [a @agent\n   166\t        fact (merge (lease/renewal (lease-id a)) (:envelope a))\n   167\t        outcome (stream/append! (get-in a [:writer :handle]) fact)]\n   168\t    (swap! agent update :holder lease/observe-renewal (:reading a) outcome)\n   169\t    outcome))\n   170\t\n   171\t\n   172\t(defn renew-if-due!\n   173\t  \"Renew when the holder's interval has been reached.  Answers true when a\n   174\t   renewal was appended.\"\n   175\t  [agent]\n   176\t  (let [a @agent]\n   177\t    (boolean\n   178\t      (when (and (holding? agent) (lease/due-to-renew? (:holder a) (:reading a)))\n   179\t        (append-renewal! agent)\n   180\t        true))))\n   181\t\n   182\t\n   183\t(defn renew!\n   184\t  \"Renew now, on a consumed input.  A holder that is not holding renews\n   185\t   nothing.\"\n   186\t  [agent]\n   187\t  (boolean (when (holding? agent) (append-renewal! agent) true)))\n   188\t\n   189\t\n   190\t(defn release!\n   191\t  \"Release on halt.  The release fact is kept until its append answers ok, so a\n   192\t   failed append retries the same fact.\"\n   193\t  [agent]\n   194\t  (let [a @agent]\n   195\t    (when (and (granted? agent) (not (get-in a [:holder :released?])))\n   196\t      (let [{:keys [holder release]} (lease/stop (:holder a))]\n   197\t        (swap! agent assoc :holder holder :release (merge release (:envelope a)))))\n   198\t    (when-let [fact (:release @agent)]\n   199\t      (when (ok? (stream/append! (get-in @agent [:writer :handle]) fact))\n   200\t        (swap! agent assoc :release nil :released-sent? true)))\n   201\t    agent))\n   202\t\n   203\t\n   204\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   205\t;; Grantor side: exchange lease\n   206\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   207\t\n   208\t(def resolver-bindings #{:per-author-media :envelope-key})\n   209\t\n   210\t(def exchange-source :egress)\n   211\t(def lineage-source :session-facts)\n   212\t(def exchange-lease-source :exchange-lease)\n   213\t(def lineage-lease-source :lineage-lease)\n   214\t(def exchange-grantor :boundary-judge)\n   215\t(def lineage-grantor :lineage-judge)\n   216\t\n   217\t\n   218\t(defn resolver\n   219\t  \"The one attribution the star compositions share.  Per-author media: the\n   220\t   source names the author.  Envelope key: the session-facts medium is written\n   221\t   only by session drivers, each stamping `:dao.star/lineage`, and that stamp\n   222\t   names the author.  A fact's own claim of authorship is never consulted.\"\n   223\t  [source fact]\n   224\t  (if (= lineage-source source)\n   225\t    (when-let [s (:dao.star/lineage fact)] {:dao.star/lineage s})\n   226\t    (case source\n   227\t      :egress :egress\n   228\t      :exchange-lease exchange-grantor\n   229\t      :lineage-lease lineage-grantor\n   230\t      nil)))\n   231\t\n   232\t\n   233\t(defn medium-declaration\n   234\t  [capacity attribution]\n   235\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity capacity\n   236\t   :value-domain :portable-values :attribution attribution})\n   237\t\n   238\t\n   239\t(defn facts-declaration\n   240\t  \"The declaration of the session-facts medium: complete history, no capacity.\"\n   241\t  []\n   242\t  {:retention :complete :value-domain :portable-values})\n   243\t\n   244\t\n   245\t(defn check-facts-declaration!\n   246\t  \"Assembly check, on the declaration and not the handle: the session-facts\n   247\t   medium must be declared `:retention :complete`.  Answers the declaration.\"\n   248\t  [decl]\n   249\t  (when-not (and (map? decl) (= :complete (:retention decl)) (not (contains? decl :capacity)))\n   250\t    (throw (ex-info \"the session-facts medium must be declared :retention :complete\"\n   251\t                    {:refused :session-facts :declaration decl})))\n   252\t  decl)\n   253\t\n   254\t\n   255\t(defn make-exchange-lease\n   256\t  \"The grantor half of the exchange lease, composed inside the peer holding the\n   257\t   HTTP boundary.  Config:\n   258\t     :ingress :egress :lease-medium  the three media (handles)\n   259\t     :tick                           the judge's tick stream (handle)\n   260\t     :open-exchanges :close-exchange the boundary's inventory and reclaim\n   261\t     :units :duration :cadence :tolerance\n   262\t     :subscription-max               required duration: the `:dao.lease/max` every\n   263\t                                     subscription exchange's grant carries, the\n   264\t                                     dead-peer bound on a host that reports\n   265\t                                     neither close nor failed write\n   266\t     :capacity                       declared capacity of the egress medium\n   267\t   The judge reads the egress medium for the responders' renewals and writes\n   268\t   grants and `:lapsed` to the lease medium.  Policy ends the lease of an\n   269\t   exchange the inventory no longer holds (peer close, gap reconciliation), and\n   270\t   reclaim is the boundary's idempotent `close-exchange`, reporting success when\n   271\t   the exchange is not open afterwards.\"\n   272\t  [{:keys [ingress egress lease-medium tick open-exchanges close-exchange\n   273\t           units duration cadence tolerance capacity subscription-max]}]\n   274\t  (when-not (lease/duration? subscription-max)\n   275\t    (throw (ex-info \"a subscription exchange needs a :dao.lease/max (:subscription-max, a duration)\"\n   276\t                    {:refused :subscription-cap :subscription-max subscription-max})))\n   277\t  (let [reclaim (fn [subject]\n   278\t                  (let [id (:http/exchange subject)]\n   279\t                    (close-exchange id)\n   280\t                    (not (contains? (open-exchanges) id))))\n   281\t        policy (fn [entry _now]\n   282\t                 (not (contains? (open-exchanges)\n   283\t                                 (:http/exchange (:subject entry)))))\n   284\t        made (lease/make-judge\n   285\t               {:units units :cadence cadence :tolerance tolerance\n   286\t                :resolver resolver :resolver-bindings resolver-bindings\n   287\t                :reclaim reclaim :policy policy\n   288\t                :writer lease-medium :self exchange-grantor\n   289\t                :ticks [{:handle tick :cursor (oldest-cursor tick)}]\n   290\t                :media [{:handle egress :cursor (oldest-cursor egress)\n   291\t                         :source exchange-source\n   292\t                         :medium (medium-declaration capacity :per-author-media)}]})]\n   293\t    (atom {:judge (:judge made) :step (:step made)\n   294\t           :ingress ingress :ingress-cursor (oldest-cursor ingress)\n   295\t           :open-exchanges open-exchanges\n   296\t           :duration duration :subscription-max subscription-max :leased #{}})))\n   297\t\n   298\t\n   299\t(defn- grant-exchange\n   300\t  \"Grant exchange `id` unsolicited.  A subscription (`/s/…`), and any exchange\n   301\t   whose kind is unknown (gap reconciliation), carries the tenure cap.\"\n   302\t  [x id subscription?]\n   303\t  (swap! x (fn [s]\n   304\t             (-> s\n   305\t                 (update :judge lease/author-grant\n   306\t                         (lease/grant (lease/mint-lease-id) {:http/exchange id}\n   307\t                                      :egress (:duration s)\n   308\t                                      (when subscription?\n   309\t                                        {:dao.lease/max (:subscription-max s)})))\n   310\t                 (update :leased conj id))))\n   311\t  x)\n   312\t\n   313\t\n   314\t(defn exchange-lease-step!\n   315\t  \"One pass: observe the ingress for each `:http/request` and grant its\n   316\t   exchange unsolicited; on an ingress gap reconcile against the inventory (an\n   317\t   open exchange without a lease is granted afresh; a leased exchange absent\n   318\t   from the inventory is ended by the judge's policy with cause `:policy`);\n   319\t   then one judge pass.  Answers the atom.\"\n   320\t  [x]\n   321\t  (let [s @x\n   322\t        r (drain (:ingress s) (:ingress-cursor s))\n   323\t        open ((:open-exchanges s))]\n   324\t    (swap! x assoc :ingress-cursor (:cursor r))\n   325\t    (doseq [v (:values r)\n   326\t            :when (= :http/request (:http/event v))\n   327\t            :let [id (:http/exchange v)]\n   328\t            :when (and (contains? open id) (not (contains? (:leased @x) id)))]\n   329\t      (grant-exchange x id (str/starts-with? (str (:http/path v)) \"/s/\")))\n   330\t    (when (:gap? r)\n   331\t      (doseq [id open :when (not (contains? (:leased @x) id))]\n   332\t        (grant-exchange x id true)))\n   333\t    ;; Forget what is closed: its lease is the judge's to end.\n   334\t    (swap! x update :leased #(into #{} (filter open) %))\n   335\t    (swap! x (fn [s] (update s :judge (:step s))))\n   336\t    x))\n   337\t\n   338\t\n   339\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   340\t;; Grantor side: lineage lease\n   341\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   342\t\n   343\t(defn make-lineage-lease\n   344\t  \"The grantor half of the lineage lease.  Config:\n   345\t     :facts          the session-facts medium (handle)\n   346\t     :lease-medium   where grants and `:lapsed` are written (handle)\n   347\t     :tick           the judge's tick stream (handle)\n   348\t     :retire!        (fn [lineage]) retiring the parked record\n   349\t     :units :duration :max :cadence :tolerance\n   350\t     :facts-declaration  the facts medium's declaration, `:retention :complete`\n   351\t   Each root fact read grants unsolicited, subject and holder\n   352\t   `{:dao.star/lineage S}`.  The judge reads the same medium for the drivers'\n   353\t   renewals and releases, attributed by the `:dao.star/lineage` envelope key.\"\n   354\t  [{:keys [lease-medium tick retire! units duration cadence tolerance]\n   355\t    cap :max session-facts :facts declaration :facts-declaration}]\n   356\t  (check-facts-declaration! declaration)\n   357\t  (let [made (lease/make-judge\n   358\t               {:units units :cadence cadence :tolerance tolerance\n   359\t                :resolver resolver :resolver-bindings resolver-bindings\n   360\t                :reclaim (fn [subject]\n   361\t                           (retire! (:dao.star/lineage subject))\n   362\t                           true)\n   363\t                :writer lease-medium :self lineage-grantor\n   364\t                :ticks [{:handle tick :cursor (oldest-cursor tick)}]\n   365\t                :media [{:handle session-facts :cursor (oldest-cursor session-facts)\n   366\t                         :source lineage-source\n   367\t                         :medium (assoc declaration :attribution :envelope-key)}]})]\n   368\t    (atom {:judge (:judge made) :step (:step made)\n   369\t           :facts session-facts :facts-cursor (oldest-cursor session-facts)\n   370\t           :duration duration :max cap})))\n   371\t\n   372\t\n   373\t(defn lineage-lease-step!\n   374\t  \"One pass: grant each newly read root, then one judge pass.\"\n   375\t  [x]\n   376\t  (let [s @x\n   377\t        r (drain (:facts s) (:facts-cursor s))]\n   378\t    (swap! x assoc :facts-cursor (:cursor r))\n   379\t    (doseq [v (:values r)\n   380\t            :when (and (map? v) (= :root (facts/fact-kind v)))\n   381\t            :let [subject {:dao.star/lineage (:dao.star/lineage v)}]]\n   382\t      (swap! x update :judge lease/author-grant\n   383\t             (lease/grant (lease/mint-lease-id) subject subject (:duration s)\n   384\t                          (when (:max s) {:dao.lease/max (:max s)}))))\n   385\t    (swap! x (fn [s] (update s :judge (:step s))))\n   386\t    x))\n     1\t(ns dao.star.router\n     2\t  \"The dao.star Mode 1 router (docs/design/dao.star.md, Routing and Sessions\n     3\t   and request kinds).\n     4\t\n     5\t   A stepped interpreter: each pass reads the ingress with its own cursor to\n     6\t   `blocked`, then drains the session-facts and lineage-lease cursors to\n     7\t   `blocked` folding them into the index, and only then classifies what the\n     8\t   ingress gave it.  Unknown is judged after both drains, never before, which\n     9\t   is what makes a just-published token impossible to answer as begin.\n    10\t\n    11\t   The router holds no token table of its own: the index is derived from the\n    12\t   two media it reads, and it forwards a request to the medium of the session\n    13\t   its token names, with every later terminal event of that exchange.  The\n    14\t   boundary never routes, and a gap forwards nothing.\"\n    15\t  (:require [dao.star.facts :as facts]\n    16\t            [dao.star.lease :as lease]\n    17\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    18\t            #?(:clj [dao.stream.remote]))\n    19\t  #?(:clj (:import [dao.stream.remote ReflectionHandle])))\n    20\t\n    21\t\n    22\t(defn- reflection?\n    23\t  [handle]\n    24\t  #?(:clj (instance? ReflectionHandle handle)\n    25\t     :default (and false handle)))\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\t(defn classify\n    29\t  \"Pure: the kind of request `(method, path)` under `index`.\n    30\t     {:kind :begin}                         `/`, or a token of an ended or\n    31\t                                            unknown lineage\n    32\t     {:kind :subscribe :lineage S}          `/s/<token>`, token live\n    33\t     {:kind :input :lineage S :token t}     `/k/<token>`, token current\n    34\t     {:kind :stale :lineage S :token t}     `/k/<token>`, token consumed\n    35\t     {:kind :unrouted}                      any other path\"\n    36\t  [index path]\n    37\t  (let [[_ head token] (re-matches #\"/(s|k)/([^/]+)\" (str path))\n    38\t        tok (when head (facts/resolve-token index token))]\n    39\t    (cond\n    40\t      (= \"/\" path) {:kind :begin}\n    41\t      (nil? head) {:kind :unrouted}\n    42\t      (contains? #{:ended :unknown} (:kind tok)) {:kind :begin}\n    43\t      (= \"s\" head) {:kind :subscribe :lineage (:lineage tok) :token token}\n    44\t      (= :current (:kind tok)) {:kind :input :lineage (:lineage tok) :token token}\n    45\t      :else {:kind :stale :lineage (:lineage tok) :token token})))\n    46\t\n    47\t\n    48\t(defn make-router\n    49\t  \"Assemble the router.  Config:\n    50\t     :ingress        the boundary's ingress medium (may be a reflection)\n    51\t     :facts          the session-facts medium, a direct handle\n    52\t     :lease          the lineage-lease medium, a direct handle\n    53\t     :begin          the begin handler's medium (handle)\n    54\t     :session-medium (fn [lineage] -> handle or nil)\n    55\t     :facts-declaration  the facts medium's declaration, `:retention :complete`\n    56\t   The facts and lease handles are classification media: a reflection answers\n    57\t   `blocked` while its request is pending, which says nothing about the source,\n    58\t   so the router refuses at assembly (ex-info `:refused :co-located`) unless\n    59\t   both are direct handles declared `:co-located? true`.\"\n    60\t  [{:keys [ingress facts lease begin session-medium co-located?] :as config}]\n    61\t  (lease/check-facts-declaration! (:facts-declaration config))\n    62\t  (when-not (and co-located?\n    63\t                 (not (reflection? facts))\n    64\t                 (not (reflection? lease)))\n    65\t    (throw (ex-info \"the router reads its classification media directly: declare :co-located? true with direct (non-reflection) handles\"\n    66\t                    {:refused :co-located})))\n    67\t  (when-not (and ingress facts lease begin (fn? session-medium))\n    68\t    (throw (ex-info \"the router needs :ingress :facts :lease :begin :session-medium\"\n    69\t                    {:refused :config :config (dissoc config :ingress :facts :lease :begin)})))\n    70\t  (atom {:config config\n    71\t         :ingress-cursor (lease/oldest-cursor ingress)\n    72\t         :facts-cursor (lease/oldest-cursor facts)\n    73\t         :lease-cursor (lease/oldest-cursor lease)\n    74\t         :index facts/empty-index\n    75\t         :routes {}\n    76\t         :gaps 0}))\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\t(defn index\n    80\t  [router]\n    81\t  (:index @router))\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t(defn- forward!\n    85\t  \"Append `message` to `handle`; a non-ok answer is loss, dropped silently.\"\n    86\t  [handle message]\n    87\t  (when handle\n    88\t    (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! handle message)))))\n    89\t\n    90\t\n    91\t(defn- route!\n    92\t  [router event]\n    93\t  (let [{:keys [config index]} @router\n    94\t        x (:http/exchange event)]\n    95\t    (case (:http/event event)\n    96\t      :http/request\n    97\t      (let [c (classify index (:http/path event))\n    98\t            target (case (:kind c)\n    99\t                     :begin (:begin config)\n   100\t                     :unrouted nil\n   101\t                     ((:session-medium config) (:lineage c)))]\n   102\t        (when (and target\n   103\t                   (forward! target {:exchange x :kind (:kind c) :token (:token c)\n   104\t                                     :lineage (:lineage c) :event event}))\n   105\t          (swap! router assoc-in [:routes x] target)))\n   106\t\n   107\t      (:http/ended :http/closed)\n   108\t      (when-let [target (get-in @router [:routes x])]\n   109\t        (swap! router update :routes dissoc x)\n   110\t        (forward! target {:exchange x :kind :terminal :event event}))\n   111\t\n   112\t      nil)))\n   113\t\n   114\t\n   115\t(defn router-step!\n   116\t  \"One pass, in the spec's order.  Answers the router.\"\n   117\t  [router]\n   118\t  (let [s @router\n   119\t        {:keys [ingress facts lease]} (:config s)\n   120\t        in (lease/drain ingress (:ingress-cursor s))\n   121\t        fs (lease/drain facts (:facts-cursor s))\n   122\t        ls (lease/drain lease (:lease-cursor s))]\n   123\t    (swap! router\n   124\t           (fn [s]\n   125\t             (-> s\n   126\t                 (assoc :ingress-cursor (:cursor in)\n   127\t                        :facts-cursor (:cursor fs)\n   128\t                        :lease-cursor (:cursor ls))\n   129\t                 (update :gaps + (if (:gap? in) 1 0))\n   130\t                 (update :index #(reduce facts/index-step % (:values fs)))\n   131\t                 (update :index #(reduce facts/index-step % (:values ls))))))\n   132\t    (doseq [event (:values in)\n   133\t            :when (map? event)]\n   134\t      (route! router event))\n   135\t    router))\n     1\t(ns dao.star.signals\n     2\t  \"Decode a request's client signals from an `:http/request` event\n     3\t   (docs/design/dao.star.md, Signals).\n     4\t\n     5\t   Signals are the client's unverified claim, so `decode` is total: a missing,\n     6\t   malformed or non-map input answers `{}` and nothing throws.  GET and DELETE\n     7\t   carry them in the query parameter the spec names, every other method in the\n     8\t   JSON body.  The JSON parse is the host's; a host without one decodes\n     9\t   nothing.\n    10\t\n    11\t   Scope: the JSON and URL-decoding seams are implemented for the JVM and\n    12\t   ClojureScript only.  On ClojureDart they are unimplemented, and `decode`\n    13\t   throws `ex-info` naming the seam (`:dao.star.signals/seam`) rather than\n    14\t   answer `{}`, which would be indistinguishable from absent signals.\"\n    15\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n    16\t            [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n    17\t            [dao.host.text :as text]\n    18\t            #?(:clj [clojure.data.json :as json])))\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\t#_{:clj-kondo/ignore [:unused-private-var]}\n    22\t(defn- unimplemented\n    23\t  [seam]\n    24\t  (throw (ex-info (str \"dao.star.signals: no \" (name seam) \" seam on this host\")\n    25\t                  {:dao.star.signals/seam seam})))\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\t(defn- parse-json\n    29\t  [s]\n    30\t  #?(:cljd (unimplemented :json)\n    31\t     :clj (json/read-str s :key-fn keyword)\n    32\t     :cljs (js->clj (js/JSON.parse s) :keywordize-keys true)))\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t(defn- url-decode\n    36\t  [s]\n    37\t  #?(:cljd (unimplemented :url-decode)\n    38\t     :clj (java.net.URLDecoder/decode ^String s \"UTF-8\")\n    39\t     :cljs (js/decodeURIComponent (str/replace s \"+\" \" \"))))\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\t(defn- body-text\n    43\t  [body]\n    44\t  (cond (string? body) body\n    45\t        (bytes/bytes? body) (text/utf8-decode body)\n    46\t        :else nil))\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(defn- query-param\n    50\t  [query k]\n    51\t  (when (string? query)\n    52\t    (some (fn [pair]\n    53\t            (let [[name value] (str/split pair #\"=\" 2)]\n    54\t              (when (= k name) (or value \"\"))))\n    55\t          (str/split query #\"&\"))))\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\t(defn decode\n    59\t  \"The signals map of request `event`, or `{}`.\"\n    60\t  [event]\n    61\t  (try\n    62\t    (let [raw (if (contains? #{:get :delete} (:http/method event))\n    63\t                (some-> (query-param (:http/query event) \"datastar\") url-decode)\n    64\t                (body-text (:http/body event)))\n    65\t          parsed (when (and (string? raw) (not (empty? raw))) (parse-json raw))]\n    66\t      (if (map? parsed) parsed {}))\n    67\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n    68\t      (if (:dao.star.signals/seam (ex-data e))\n    69\t        (throw e)\n    70\t        {}))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/driver.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.star.driver\n     2\t  \"The dao.star Mode 1 driver (docs/design/dao.star.md, Flow and Liveness).\n     3\t\n     4\t   Per session the driver parks a real `yin.vm` continuation through\n     5\t   `dao.await`: one VM per session, whose program is pure sequential logic\n     6\t   reading its input medium (`in`) and emitting model values on its view medium\n     7\t   (`out`).  The driver does all the I/O.  It reads the session's routed\n     8\t   inputs with its own cursor, steps the parked continuation, drains the view\n     9\t   medium for the new model, mints the successor occurrence, appends the\n    10\t   consumption fact, and only after that append answers `ok` projects the\n    11\t   model to the egress medium.  The program never appends an effect.\n    12\t\n    13\t   Projection is the composition's pure `(project-fn occurrence-id model)`,\n    14\t   answering the complete SSE wire text; the root begin page is a separate\n    15\t   `(begin-fn lineage)`.  Subscribe and stale requests re-project the stored\n    16\t   latest `{:occurrence O :model m}` without resuming the VM.\n    17\t\n    18\t   The driver observes its grants before it consumes or projects, renews the\n    19\t   lineage lease on each consumed input and on its tick while a subscription is\n    20\t   open, stops at its bound (an input arriving then is handled as begin), and\n    21\t   releases on halt.\"\n    22\t  (:require [dao.await :as await]\n    23\t            [dao.star.facts :as facts]\n    24\t            [dao.star.lease :as lease]\n    25\t            [dao.star.signals :as signals]\n    26\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    27\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]))\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\t(defn- ok?\n    31\t  [r]\n    32\t  (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t(defn- new-ring\n    36\t  [capacity]\n    37\t  (let [r (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n    38\t                         ring/capacity-key capacity})]\n    39\t    (when-not (ok? r) (throw (ex-info \"cannot create a session medium\" {:outcome r})))\n    40\t    (:dao.stream/handle r)))\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\t(defn make-driver\n    44\t  \"Assemble the driver.  Config:\n    45\t     :facts :egress :begin     media handles (the session-facts writer, the\n    46\t                               egress writer, the begin handler's medium)\n    47\t     :tick                     the drivers' tick stream (handle)\n    48\t     :lineage-lease            the lineage-lease medium (handle, read for grants)\n    49\t     :exchange-lease           the exchange-lease medium (handle, read for grants)\n    50\t     :program                  a `dao.await` process reading `in`, writing `out`\n    51\t     :project-fn :begin-fn     the composition's projections\n    52\t     :units :lineage-renewal-interval :exchange-renewal-interval\n    53\t     :session-capacity         declared capacity of each session medium\n    54\t     :facts-declaration        the session-facts medium's declaration; refused\n    55\t                               (`:refused :session-facts`) unless\n    56\t                               `:retention :complete`\n    57\t     :lease-capacity           declared capacity of the lease media\"\n    58\t  [{:keys [program project-fn begin-fn] :as config}]\n    59\t  (when-not (and (map? program) (fn? project-fn) (fn? begin-fn))\n    60\t    (throw (ex-info \"the driver needs :program, :project-fn and :begin-fn\"\n    61\t                    {:refused :config})))\n    62\t  (lease/check-facts-declaration! (:facts-declaration config))\n    63\t  (atom {:config config\n    64\t         :begin-cursor (lease/oldest-cursor (:begin config))\n    65\t         :sessions {}}))\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\t(defn session-medium\n    69\t  \"The routed-input medium of lineage `s`, or nil: the router's forward target.\"\n    70\t  [driver s]\n    71\t  (get-in @driver [:sessions s :medium]))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t(defn sessions\n    75\t  [driver]\n    76\t  (set (keys (:sessions @driver))))\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\t(defn latest\n    80\t  \"The session's stored latest `{:occurrence O :model m}`, or nil.\"\n    81\t  [driver s]\n    82\t  (get-in @driver [:sessions s :latest]))\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\t(defn subscriptions\n    86\t  \"The exchange ids the session currently holds open as subscriptions.\"\n    87\t  [driver s]\n    88\t  (set (keys (get-in @driver [:sessions s :subs]))))\n    89\t\n    90\t\n    91\t(defn lineage-agent\n    92\t  [driver s]\n    93\t  (get-in @driver [:sessions s :agent]))\n    94\t\n    95\t\n    96\t(defn retire!\n    97\t  \"Retire the parked record of lineage `s`: the VM result and its media handles.\n    98\t   The reclaim procedure of the lineage lease; facts are never touched.\"\n    99\t  [driver s]\n   100\t  (swap! driver update :sessions dissoc s)\n   101\t  driver)\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   105\t;; Effects out\n   106\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   107\t\n   108\t(defn- emit!\n   109\t  [config effects]\n   110\t  (doseq [e effects]\n   111\t    (stream/append! (:egress config) e)))\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\t(defn- head\n   115\t  [x type]\n   116\t  {:http/exchange x :http/effect :http/head :http/status 200\n   117\t   :http/headers {\"content-type\" type \"cache-control\" \"no-cache\"}})\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\t(defn- chunk-fx\n   121\t  [x body]\n   122\t  {:http/exchange x :http/effect :http/chunk :http/body body})\n   123\t\n   124\t\n   125\t(defn- end\n   126\t  [x]\n   127\t  {:http/exchange x :http/effect :http/end})\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(defn- answer!\n   131\t  \"Head, one SSE projection, end: the reply to a one-shot exchange.\"\n   132\t  [config x occurrence model]\n   133\t  (emit! config [(head x \"text/event-stream\")\n   134\t                 (chunk-fx x ((:project-fn config) occurrence model))\n   135\t                 (end x)]))\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\t(defn- patch!\n   139\t  [config s]\n   140\t  (let [{:keys [occurrence model]} (:latest s)]\n   141\t    (doseq [x (keys (:subs s))\n   142\t            :when (not (contains? (:sub-staged s) x))]\n   143\t      (emit! config [(chunk-fx x ((:project-fn config) occurrence model))]))))\n   144\t\n   145\t\n   146\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   147\t;; Session construction\n   148\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   149\t\n   150\t(defn- decl\n   151\t  [capacity attribution]\n   152\t  (lease/medium-declaration capacity attribution))\n   153\t\n   154\t\n   155\t(defn- lineage-agent-config\n   156\t  [{:keys [tick lineage-lease facts units lineage-renewal-interval lease-capacity\n   157\t           facts-declaration]} s]\n   158\t  (let [subject {:dao.star/lineage s}]\n   159\t    {:self subject :grantor lease/lineage-grantor :subject subject\n   160\t     :units units :renewal-interval lineage-renewal-interval\n   161\t     :resolver lease/resolver :resolver-bindings lease/resolver-bindings\n   162\t     :tick tick\n   163\t     :fact {:handle lineage-lease :source lease/lineage-lease-source\n   164\t            :medium (decl lease-capacity :per-author-media)}\n   165\t     :writer {:handle facts :medium (assoc facts-declaration :attribution :envelope-key)}\n   166\t     :envelope {:dao.star/lineage s}}))\n   167\t\n   168\t\n   169\t(defn- exchange-agent-config\n   170\t  [{:keys [tick exchange-lease egress units exchange-renewal-interval lease-capacity]} x]\n   171\t  {:self :egress :grantor lease/exchange-grantor :subject {:http/exchange x}\n   172\t   :units units :renewal-interval exchange-renewal-interval\n   173\t   :resolver lease/resolver :resolver-bindings lease/resolver-bindings\n   174\t   :tick tick\n   175\t   :fact {:handle exchange-lease :source lease/exchange-lease-source\n   176\t          :medium (decl lease-capacity :per-author-media)}\n   177\t   :writer {:handle egress :medium (decl lease-capacity :per-author-media)}})\n   178\t\n   179\t\n   180\t(defn- last-model\n   181\t  \"Drain the view medium: the newest model emitted, the advanced cursor, and\n   182\t   whether the cursor answered a gap.\"\n   183\t  [handle cursor]\n   184\t  (let [r (lease/drain handle cursor)]\n   185\t    {:cursor (:cursor r) :model (last (:values r)) :emitted? (seq (:values r))\n   186\t     :gap? (:gap? r)}))\n   187\t\n   188\t\n   189\t(defn- update-session!\n   190\t  [driver s f & args]\n   191\t  (swap! driver (fn [d] (if (contains? (:sessions d) s)\n   192\t                          (apply update-in d [:sessions s] f args)\n   193\t                          d))))\n   194\t\n   195\t\n   196\t(defn- forget!\n   197\t  \"A gap on a medium the session reads: forget every subscription and renew\n   198\t   nothing from then on.  The lineage's holder is marked gapped, so it renews\n   199\t   no lease; the leases lapse by silence.\"\n   200\t  [driver s]\n   201\t  (when-let [sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])]\n   202\t    (swap! (:agent sess) assoc :gapped? true)\n   203\t    (update-session! driver s assoc :subs {} :sub-staged #{})))\n   204\t\n   205\t\n   206\t(defn- begin!\n   207\t  \"Begin a lineage for exchange `x`: a fresh session with its own VM, the root\n   208\t   fact appended before anything is answered.  The begin page itself is staged\n   209\t   until the lineage grant has been observed (`flush-begin!`).  A root fact that\n   210\t   is not accepted starts nothing and answers nothing; the exchange lapses by\n   211\t   silence.\"\n   212\t  [driver x]\n   213\t  (let [{:keys [program facts] :as config} (:config @driver)\n   214\t        s (str (random-uuid))\n   215\t        in (new-ring (:session-capacity config))\n   216\t        out (new-ring (:session-capacity config))\n   217\t        medium (new-ring (:session-capacity config))\n   218\t        result (await/run (update program :env merge {'in in 'out out}))\n   219\t        {:keys [cursor model]} (last-model out (lease/oldest-cursor out))]\n   220\t    (when (ok? (stream/append! facts (facts/root s)))\n   221\t      (swap! driver assoc-in [:sessions s]\n   222\t             {:lineage s :medium medium :cursor (lease/oldest-cursor medium)\n   223\t              :vm-in in :vm-out out :out-cursor cursor :result result\n   224\t              :latest {:occurrence s :model model} :subs {} :sub-staged #{}\n   225\t              :begin-pending x\n   226\t              :agent (lease/make-agent (lineage-agent-config config s))}))))\n   227\t\n   228\t\n   229\t(defn begin-step!\n   230\t  \"Read the begin medium to `blocked`, beginning a lineage per message.  A gap\n   231\t   on it loses begin requests; every session forgets its subscriptions.\"\n   232\t  [driver]\n   233\t  (let [{:keys [config begin-cursor]} @driver\n   234\t        r (lease/drain (:begin config) begin-cursor)]\n   235\t    (swap! driver assoc :begin-cursor (:cursor r))\n   236\t    (when (:gap? r)\n   237\t      (doseq [s (sessions driver)] (forget! driver s)))\n   238\t    (doseq [m (:values r)\n   239\t            :when (and (map? m) (= :begin (:kind m)) (:exchange m))]\n   240\t      (begin! driver (:exchange m)))\n   241\t    driver))\n   242\t\n   243\t\n   244\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   245\t;; One session\n   246\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   247\t\n   248\t(defn- flush-begin!\n   249\t  \"Answer the staged begin page once the lineage grant is observed and the\n   250\t   holder is holding; drop it if the lease is already past its bound.\"\n   251\t  [driver s]\n   252\t  (let [{:keys [config]} @driver\n   253\t        sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])\n   254\t        x (:begin-pending sess)]\n   255\t    (when x\n   256\t      (cond\n   257\t        (lease/past-bound? (:agent sess)) (update-session! driver s dissoc :begin-pending)\n   258\t        (lease/holding? (:agent sess))\n   259\t        (do (update-session! driver s dissoc :begin-pending)\n   260\t            (emit! config [(head x \"text/html\")\n   261\t                           (chunk-fx x ((:begin-fn config) s))\n   262\t                           (end x)]))))))\n   263\t\n   264\t\n   265\t(defn- publish!\n   266\t  \"Append the pending transition's fact; only when it answers `ok` does the new\n   267\t   occurrence become the latest and any UI carrying its id get projected.  The\n   268\t   holder's tenure is rechecked first, fail closed: a holder past its bound or\n   269\t   lapsed drops the staged transition (its exchange is left to lapse and the\n   270\t   requester sees silence); a holder not holding for any other reason (a gap)\n   271\t   keeps it staged and publishes nothing.\"\n   272\t  [driver s]\n   273\t  (let [{:keys [config]} @driver\n   274\t        sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])\n   275\t        {:keys [successor predecessor model exchange halted?]} (:unpublished sess)\n   276\t        agent (:agent sess)]\n   277\t    (when (and sess (:unpublished sess))\n   278\t      (cond\n   279\t        (lease/past-bound? agent)\n   280\t        (update-session! driver s dissoc :unpublished)\n   281\t\n   282\t        (not (lease/holding? agent)) nil\n   283\t\n   284\t        :else\n   285\t        (let [fact (if halted?\n   286\t                     (facts/ended s :halted)\n   287\t                     (facts/consumption s successor predecessor))]\n   288\t          (when (ok? (stream/append! (:facts config) fact))\n   289\t            (update-session! driver s\n   290\t                             (fn [x] (-> x\n   291\t                                         (dissoc :unpublished)\n   292\t                                         (cond-> (not halted?)\n   293\t                                           (assoc :latest {:occurrence successor :model model})))))\n   294\t            (let [sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])\n   295\t                  occ (if halted? predecessor successor)]\n   296\t              (answer! config exchange occ model)\n   297\t              (when-not halted? (patch! config sess))\n   298\t              (if halted?\n   299\t                (lease/release! agent)\n   300\t                (lease/renew! agent)))))))))\n   301\t\n   302\t\n   303\t(defn- consume!\n   304\t  \"Step the parked continuation with one input and stage its successor.  Every\n   305\t   consumed input yields a successor, whether or not the program emitted a new\n   306\t   model: when it did not, the previous model is retained.\"\n   307\t  [driver s m]\n   308\t  (let [sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])\n   309\t        input {:signals (signals/decode (:event m))}]\n   310\t    (stream/append! (:vm-in sess) input)\n   311\t    (let [result (await/resume (:result sess))\n   312\t          {:keys [cursor model emitted? gap?]} (last-model (:vm-out sess) (:out-cursor sess))]\n   313\t      (update-session! driver s assoc :result result :out-cursor cursor\n   314\t                       :unpublished {:successor (str (random-uuid))\n   315\t                                     :predecessor (get-in sess [:latest :occurrence])\n   316\t                                     :model (if emitted? model (get-in sess [:latest :model]))\n   317\t                                     :exchange (:exchange m)\n   318\t                                     :halted? (not (:blocked? result))})\n   319\t      (when gap? (forget! driver s))\n   320\t      (publish! driver s))))\n   321\t\n   322\t\n   323\t(defn- subscribe!\n   324\t  \"Open the subscription: its holder starts observing its exchange grant now,\n   325\t   and the head and first projection are staged until the grant is observed.\"\n   326\t  [driver s m]\n   327\t  (let [{:keys [config]} @driver\n   328\t        x (:exchange m)]\n   329\t    (update-session! driver s\n   330\t                     (fn [sess]\n   331\t                       (-> sess\n   332\t                           (assoc-in [:subs x] (lease/make-agent (exchange-agent-config config x)))\n   333\t                           (update :sub-staged conj x))))))\n   334\t\n   335\t\n   336\t(defn- flush-subscriptions!\n   337\t  \"Project the current occurrence to each staged subscription whose exchange\n   338\t   holder is now holding.\"\n   339\t  [driver s]\n   340\t  (let [{:keys [config]} @driver]\n   341\t    (doseq [x (:sub-staged (get-in @driver [:sessions s]))\n   342\t            :let [a (get-in @driver [:sessions s :subs x])]\n   343\t            :when (and a (lease/holding? a))]\n   344\t      (let [{:keys [occurrence model]} (get-in @driver [:sessions s :latest])]\n   345\t        (update-session! driver s update :sub-staged disj x)\n   346\t        (emit! config [(head x \"text/event-stream\")\n   347\t                       (chunk-fx x ((:project-fn config) occurrence model))])))))\n   348\t\n   349\t\n   350\t(defn- handle!\n   351\t  \"Handle one routed message.  Answers :wait when the message must stay unread\n   352\t   (no grant observed yet, or the holder is not holding for a reason short of\n   353\t   its bound), :consumed otherwise.  Leased actions are gated on `holding?`,\n   354\t   which fails closed on a missing or invalid reading and on a gap.\"\n   355\t  [driver s m]\n   356\t  (let [{:keys [config]} @driver\n   357\t        sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])\n   358\t        agent (:agent sess)]\n   359\t    (cond\n   360\t      (= :terminal (:kind m))\n   361\t      (do (update-session! driver s (fn [x] (-> x\n   362\t                                                (update :subs dissoc (:exchange m))\n   363\t                                                (update :sub-staged disj (:exchange m)))))\n   364\t          :consumed)\n   365\t\n   366\t      (not (lease/granted? agent)) :wait\n   367\t\n   368\t      (lease/past-bound? agent)\n   369\t      (do (begin! driver (:exchange m)) :consumed)\n   370\t\n   371\t      (not (lease/holding? agent)) :wait\n   372\t\n   373\t      (= :subscribe (:kind m)) (do (subscribe! driver s m) :consumed)\n   374\t\n   375\t      (and (= :input (:kind m))\n   376\t           (= (:token m) (get-in sess [:latest :occurrence])))\n   377\t      (do (consume! driver s m) :consumed)\n   378\t\n   379\t      :else\n   380\t      (let [{:keys [occurrence model]} (:latest sess)]\n   381\t        (answer! config (:exchange m) occurrence model)\n   382\t        :consumed))))\n   383\t\n   384\t\n   385\t(defn- read-messages!\n   386\t  [driver s]\n   387\t  (loop []\n   388\t    (let [sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])]\n   389\t      (when (and sess (not (:unpublished sess)))\n   390\t        (let [r (stream/next (:medium sess) (:cursor sess))]\n   391\t          (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   392\t            :dao.stream/ok\n   393\t            (when (= :consumed (handle! driver s (:dao.stream/value r)))\n   394\t              (update-session! driver s assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   395\t              (recur))\n   396\t\n   397\t            :dao.stream/gap\n   398\t            (do (update-session! driver s assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   399\t                (forget! driver s)\n   400\t                (recur))\n   401\t\n   402\t            nil))))))\n   403\t\n   404\t\n   405\t(defn- tick-subscriptions!\n   406\t  \"On the tick: each subscription's holder observes its grant and any lapse,\n   407\t   and renews when due; a lapsed or gapped exchange is dropped.\"\n   408\t  [driver s]\n   409\t  (let [sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])]\n   410\t    (doseq [[x a] (:subs sess)]\n   411\t      (lease/step! a)\n   412\t      (if (or (:lapsed? @a) (:gapped? @a) (lease/past-bound? a))\n   413\t        (update-session! driver s (fn [y] (-> y (update :subs dissoc x) (update :sub-staged disj x))))\n   414\t        (lease/renew-if-due! a)))\n   415\t    (flush-subscriptions! driver s)\n   416\t    (when (seq (:subs (get-in @driver [:sessions s])))\n   417\t      (lease/renew-if-due! (:agent sess)))))\n   418\t\n   419\t\n   420\t(defn session-step!\n   421\t  [driver s]\n   422\t  (when-let [sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])]\n   423\t    (let [agent (:agent sess)]\n   424\t      (lease/step! agent)\n   425\t      (when (lease/gapped? agent) (forget! driver s))\n   426\t      (flush-begin! driver s)\n   427\t      (when (lease/release-pending? agent) (lease/release! agent))\n   428\t      (when (:unpublished sess) (publish! driver s))\n   429\t      (read-messages! driver s)\n   430\t      (tick-subscriptions! driver s)))\n   431\t  driver)\n   432\t\n   433\t\n   434\t(defn driver-step!\n   435\t  \"One pass: begin handler, then every session.  Answers the driver.\"\n   436\t  [driver]\n   437\t  (begin-step! driver)\n   438\t  (doseq [s (sessions driver)]\n   439\t    (session-step! driver s))\n   440\t  driver)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/http.cljc | sed -n '115,385p'; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(deftest|swap-vals|interleav|single-pass|renewal|gap|cap|512|release|tick' test/dao/star/*_test.clj test/dao/stream/http_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/http.cljc | sed -n '115,385p'; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(deftest|swap-vals|interleav|single-pass|renewal|gap|cap|512|release|tick' test/dao/star/*_test.clj test/dao/stream/http_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"   115\t    (seam-ok? close!)))\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\t(defn- terminal-event\n   119\t  [id event]\n   120\t  {:http/exchange id :http/event event})\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn- finish!\n   124\t  \"Deposit the one terminal event of an already-claimed exchange.  An exchange\n   125\t   whose request event is still being deposited has its terminal parked in the\n   126\t   `:awaiting` slot; `accept!` deposits it straight after the request.  Which\n   127\t   side deposits is decided by the committed transition (`swap-vals!`): the\n   128\t   event parks only if the committed prior state still held the slot, and a\n   129\t   slot `accept!` already removed means this call deposits directly.\"\n   130\t  [boundary id entry event]\n   131\t  (if (:requested? entry)\n   132\t    (deposit! boundary (terminal-event id event))\n   133\t    (let [[old _] (swap-vals! (:state boundary)\n   134\t                              (fn [s]\n   135\t                                (cond-> s\n   136\t                                  (contains? (:awaiting s) id)\n   137\t                                  (assoc-in [:awaiting id] event))))]\n   138\t      (when-not (contains? (:awaiting old) id)\n   139\t        (deposit! boundary (terminal-event id event))))))\n   140\t\n   141\t\n   142\t(defn- claim!\n   143\t  \"Atomically remove exchange `id` from the open set; its entry, or nil when\n   144\t   this boundary does not hold it open.  Ownership is the committed transition:\n   145\t   the entry is read from the state the successful swap replaced, so of any\n   146\t   number of competing claims exactly one answers non-nil.\"\n   147\t  [boundary id]\n   148\t  (let [[old _] (swap-vals! (:state boundary) update :open dissoc id)]\n   149\t    (get-in old [:open id])))\n   150\t\n   151\t\n   152\t(defn- close-claimed!\n   153\t  \"Observably gone: drop the socket this boundary holds and deposit the\n   154\t   terminal `:http/closed`.\"\n   155\t  [boundary id entry]\n   156\t  (drop-socket! entry)\n   157\t  (finish! boundary id entry :http/closed))\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\t(defn close-exchange\n   161\t  \"The idempotent reclaim procedure for a `dao.lease.md` judge composed inside\n   162\t   this boundary: close the socket of exchange `id` and deposit its terminal\n   163\t   `:http/closed`.  Answers true when it closed an open exchange, false when\n   164\t   there was none.  Not for code written against the contract.\"\n   165\t  [boundary id]\n   166\t  (if-let [entry (claim! boundary id)]\n   167\t    (do (close-claimed! boundary id entry) true)\n   168\t    false))\n   169\t\n   170\t\n   171\t(defn open-exchanges\n   172\t  \"The ids of the exchanges currently held open, the inventory a\n   173\t   `dao.lease.md` judge needs after a restart or an ingress `gap`.\"\n   174\t  [boundary]\n   175\t  (set (keys (:open @(:state boundary)))))\n   176\t\n   177\t\n   178\t(defn- close-all!\n   179\t  [boundary]\n   180\t  (doseq [id (open-exchanges boundary)]\n   181\t    (close-exchange boundary id)))\n   182\t\n   183\t\n   184\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   185\t;; Events in\n   186\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   187\t\n   188\t(defn- none?\n   189\t  [x]\n   190\t  (or (nil? x)\n   191\t      (and (string? x) (empty? x))\n   192\t      (and (bytes/bytes? x) (zero? (bytes/length x)))))\n   193\t\n   194\t\n   195\t(defn- request-event\n   196\t  [id {:keys [method path query headers body]}]\n   197\t  (cond-> {:http/exchange id\n   198\t           :http/event :http/request\n   199\t           :http/method (keyword (str/lower-case (name method)))\n   200\t           :http/path path\n   201\t           :http/headers (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(str/lower-case (str k)) v])) headers)}\n   202\t    (not (none? query)) (assoc :http/query query)\n   203\t    (not (none? body)) (assoc :http/body body)))\n   204\t\n   205\t\n   206\t(defn- body-size\n   207\t  [body]\n   208\t  (cond (nil? body) 0\n   209\t        (string? body) (bytes/length (text/utf8-encode body))\n   210\t        :else (bytes/length body)))\n   211\t\n   212\t\n   213\t(defn accept!\n   214\t  \"Adapter entry: one valid, framed request arrived with its `socket` seam.\n   215\t   `request` is `{:method :path :query :headers :body}` as the host parsed it.\n   216\t   Answers `{:http/status :http/accepted :http/exchange id}`, or\n   217\t   `{:http/status :http/full}`, `:http/too-large` or `:http/stopped` when the\n   218\t   request must be answered below the transform (503, 413, 503) and was not\n   219\t   deposited.  When the request event cannot be deposited the exchange's socket\n   220\t   is closed with no synthesized response and `{:http/status :http/gone}` is\n   221\t   answered.\"\n   222\t  [boundary request socket]\n   223\t  (cond\n   224\t    (> (body-size (:body request)) (:max-body-bytes boundary))\n   225\t    {:http/status :http/too-large}\n   226\t\n   227\t    :else\n   228\t    (let [outcome (volatile! nil)\n   229\t          id (volatile! nil)]\n   230\t      (swap! (:state boundary)\n   231\t             (fn [s]\n   232\t               (cond\n   233\t                 (:stopped? s) (do (vreset! outcome :http/stopped) s)\n   234\t                 (>= (count (:open s)) (:max-open boundary))\n   235\t                 (do (vreset! outcome :http/full) s)\n   236\t                 :else\n   237\t                 (let [n (inc (:n s))\n   238\t                       xid [(:incarnation boundary) n]]\n   239\t                   (vreset! outcome :http/accepted)\n   240\t                   (vreset! id xid)\n   241\t                   (-> s\n   242\t                       (assoc :n n)\n   243\t                       (assoc-in [:open xid] {:socket socket :phase :new\n   244\t                                              :requested? false})\n   245\t                       (assoc-in [:awaiting xid] nil))))))\n   246\t      (if-not (= :http/accepted @outcome)\n   247\t        {:http/status @outcome}\n   248\t        (let [xid @id\n   249\t              ok? (deposit! boundary (request-event xid request))]\n   250\t          (if-not ok?\n   251\t            ;; Nowhere to land: the terminal event has none either.\n   252\t            (let [entry (claim! boundary xid)]\n   253\t              (swap! (:state boundary) update :awaiting dissoc xid)\n   254\t              (when entry (drop-socket! entry))\n   255\t              {:http/status :http/gone :http/exchange xid})\n   256\t            (let [[old _] (swap-vals! (:state boundary)\n   257\t                                      (fn [s]\n   258\t                                        (cond-> (update s :awaiting dissoc xid)\n   259\t                                          (contains? (:open s) xid)\n   260\t                                          (assoc-in [:open xid :requested?] true))))]\n   261\t              (when-let [event (get-in old [:awaiting xid])]\n   262\t                (deposit! boundary (terminal-event xid event)))\n   263\t              {:http/status :http/accepted :http/exchange xid})))))))\n   264\t\n   265\t\n   266\t(defn peer-closed!\n   267\t  \"Adapter entry: the peer (or the connection) went away.  Deposits the\n   268\t   terminal `:http/closed` once; a no-op for an exchange no longer open.\"\n   269\t  [boundary id]\n   270\t  (close-exchange boundary id))\n   271\t\n   272\t\n   273\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   274\t;; Effects out\n   275\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   276\t\n   277\t(defn- effect?\n   278\t  [v]\n   279\t  (and (map? v) (contains? v :http/exchange) (keyword? (:http/effect v))))\n   280\t\n   281\t\n   282\t(defn- chunk-payload?\n   283\t  [x]\n   284\t  (or (string? x) (bytes/bytes? x)))\n   285\t\n   286\t\n   287\t(defn- perform!\n   288\t  \"Perform one effect for an exchange this boundary holds open.\"\n   289\t  [boundary id entry effect]\n   290\t  (let [socket (:socket entry)\n   291\t        phase (:phase entry)\n   292\t        fail! (fn [] (when-let [e (claim! boundary id)] (close-claimed! boundary id e)))\n   293\t        set-phase! (fn [p] (swap! (:state boundary)\n   294\t                                  (fn [s] (if (contains? (:open s) id)\n   295\t                                            (assoc-in s [:open id :phase] p)\n   296\t                                            s))))]\n   297\t    (case (:http/effect effect)\n   298\t      :http/head\n   299\t      (if (and (= :new phase) (integer? (:http/status effect)))\n   300\t        (if (seam-ok? (:head! socket) (:http/status effect) (or (:http/headers effect) {}))\n   301\t          (set-phase! :streaming)\n   302\t          (fail!))\n   303\t        (fail!))\n   304\t\n   305\t      :http/chunk\n   306\t      (if (and (= :streaming phase) (chunk-payload? (:http/body effect)))\n   307\t        (when-not (seam-ok? (:write! socket) (:http/body effect))\n   308\t          (fail!))\n   309\t        (fail!))\n   310\t\n   311\t      :http/end\n   312\t      (if (= :streaming phase)\n   313\t        (when-let [e (claim! boundary id)]\n   314\t          (if (seam-ok? (:end! socket))\n   315\t            (finish! boundary id e :http/ended)\n   316\t            (close-claimed! boundary id e)))\n   317\t        (fail!))\n   318\t\n   319\t      ;; An effect kind this interpreter does not know is not its own.\n   320\t      nil)))\n   321\t\n   322\t\n   323\t(defn- stop-listener!\n   324\t  [boundary]\n   325\t  (when-let [f (:on-stop @(:state boundary))]\n   326\t    (try (f) (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))))\n   327\t\n   328\t\n   329\t(defn stop!\n   330\t  \"Boundary stop: close every open exchange (each deposits `:http/closed`),\n   331\t   refuse further requests, and stop the listener.  Idempotent.\"\n   332\t  [boundary]\n   333\t  (swap! (:state boundary) assoc :stopped? true)\n   334\t  (close-all! boundary)\n   335\t  (stop-listener! boundary)\n   336\t  boundary)\n   337\t\n   338\t\n   339\t(defn on-stop!\n   340\t  \"Register the host listener's stop function, run when the boundary stops or\n   341\t   its egress medium ends.\"\n   342\t  [boundary f]\n   343\t  (swap! (:state boundary) assoc :on-stop f)\n   344\t  boundary)\n   345\t\n   346\t\n   347\t(defn egress-step\n   348\t  \"Perform the effects the egress medium holds, in its order, until it has\n   349\t   none more; never waits.  Answers the boundary.\"\n   350\t  [boundary]\n   351\t  (loop []\n   352\t    (let [s @(:state boundary)]\n   353\t      (when-not (:stopped? s)\n   354\t        (let [r (stream/next (:egress boundary) (:cursor s))\n   355\t              outcome (:dao.stream/outcome r)]\n   356\t          (condp = outcome\n   357\t            :dao.stream/ok\n   358\t            (do (swap! (:state boundary) assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   359\t                (let [v (:dao.stream/value r)]\n   360\t                  (when (effect? v)\n   361\t                    (let [id (:http/exchange v)]\n   362\t                      (when-let [entry (get-in @(:state boundary) [:open id])]\n   363\t                        (perform! boundary id entry v)))))\n   364\t                (recur))\n   365\t\n   366\t            :dao.stream/blocked nil\n   367\t\n   368\t            ;; The step cannot say whose effects were lost.\n   369\t            :dao.stream/gap\n   370\t            (do (close-all! boundary)\n   371\t                (swap! (:state boundary) assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   372\t                (recur))\n   373\t\n   374\t            ;; end, transport-error, or anything else: it can never answer again.\n   375\t            (stop! boundary))))))\n   376\t  boundary)\ntest/dao/star/peer_close_test.clj:9:(deftest a-peer-close-is-read-as-data-and-drops-the-subscription\ntest/dao/star/signals_test.clj:9:(deftest get-and-delete-read-the-query-parameter\ntest/dao/star/signals_test.clj:17:(deftest other-methods-read-the-json-body\ntest/dao/star/signals_test.clj:22:(deftest decode-is-total\ntest/dao/star/signals_test.clj:37:(deftest a-get-ignores-the-body-and-a-post-ignores-the-query\ntest/dao/star/r2_test.clj:3:   fail-closed tenure checks, consumption independent of emission, gap\ntest/dao/star/r2_test.clj:4:   handling on every medium, grants published before a holder's first tick,\ntest/dao/star/r2_test.clj:5:   failed-release retry, and the strengthened order and bound tests.\"\ntest/dao/star/r2_test.clj:18:(defn- tick-only!\ntest/dao/star/r2_test.clj:19:  \"Move only the named tick streams (keys of `(:ticks w)`) to `now` and pump.\"\ntest/dao/star/r2_test.clj:22:    (stream/append! (get-in w [:ticks k]) (dl/tick {:ms now})))\ntest/dao/star/r2_test.clj:36:(defn- renewals\ntest/dao/star/r2_test.clj:38:  (count (filter #(= :dao.lease/renewal (:dao.lease/event %)) (h/values (:egress w)))))\ntest/dao/star/r2_test.clj:50:(deftest the-begin-page-waits-for-the-lineage-grant-to-be-observed\ntest/dao/star/r2_test.clj:52:    ;; the judges tick, the driver has no reading yet\ntest/dao/star/r2_test.clj:53:    (tick-only! w [:exchange :lineage] 10)\ntest/dao/star/r2_test.clj:58:      (tick-only! w [:driver] 10)\ntest/dao/star/r2_test.clj:63:(deftest an-input-waits-while-the-holder-has-no-reading\ntest/dao/star/r2_test.clj:68:    (testing \"a session whose driver never ticks consumes nothing\"\ntest/dao/star/r2_test.clj:69:      (tick-only! w2 [:exchange :lineage] 10)\ntest/dao/star/r2_test.clj:80:(deftest a-subscription-projection-waits-for-its-exchange-grant