{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/http.cljc | sed -n '120,160p;235,265p'; nl -ba test/dao/stream/http_test.clj | sed -n '380,465p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/signals.cljc; nl -ba test/dao/star/r2_test.clj | sed -n '45,145p;185,350p'\"","aggregated_output":"   120\t  {:http/exchange id :http/event event})\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn- finish!\n   124\t  \"Deposit the one terminal event of an already-claimed exchange.  An exchange\n   125\t   whose request event is still being deposited has its terminal parked in the\n   126\t   `:awaiting` slot; `accept!` deposits it straight after the request.  Which\n   127\t   side deposits is decided by the committed transition (`swap-vals!`): the\n   128\t   event parks only if the committed prior state still held the slot, and a\n   129\t   slot `accept!` already removed means this call deposits directly.\"\n   130\t  [boundary id entry event]\n   131\t  (if (:requested? entry)\n   132\t    (deposit! boundary (terminal-event id event))\n   133\t    (let [[old _] (swap-vals! (:state boundary)\n   134\t                              (fn [s]\n   135\t                                (cond-> s\n   136\t                                  (contains? (:awaiting s) id)\n   137\t                                  (assoc-in [:awaiting id] event))))]\n   138\t      (when-not (contains? (:awaiting old) id)\n   139\t        (deposit! boundary (terminal-event id event))))))\n   140\t\n   141\t\n   142\t(defn- claim!\n   143\t  \"Atomically remove exchange `id` from the open set; its entry, or nil when\n   144\t   this boundary does not hold it open.  Ownership is the committed transition:\n   145\t   the entry is read from the state the successful swap replaced, so of any\n   146\t   number of competing claims exactly one answers non-nil.\"\n   147\t  [boundary id]\n   148\t  (let [[old _] (swap-vals! (:state boundary) update :open dissoc id)]\n   149\t    (get-in old [:open id])))\n   150\t\n   151\t\n   152\t(defn- close-claimed!\n   153\t  \"Observably gone: drop the socket this boundary holds and deposit the\n   154\t   terminal `:http/closed`.\"\n   155\t  [boundary id entry]\n   156\t  (drop-socket! entry)\n   157\t  (finish! boundary id entry :http/closed))\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\t(defn close-exchange\n   235\t                 (do (vreset! outcome :http/full) s)\n   236\t                 :else\n   237\t                 (let [n (inc (:n s))\n   238\t                       xid [(:incarnation boundary) n]]\n   239\t                   (vreset! outcome :http/accepted)\n   240\t                   (vreset! id xid)\n   241\t                   (-> s\n   242\t                       (assoc :n n)\n   243\t                       (assoc-in [:open xid] {:socket socket :phase :new\n   244\t                                              :requested? false})\n   245\t                       (assoc-in [:awaiting xid] nil))))))\n   246\t      (if-not (= :http/accepted @outcome)\n   247\t        {:http/status @outcome}\n   248\t        (let [xid @id\n   249\t              ok? (deposit! boundary (request-event xid request))]\n   250\t          (if-not ok?\n   251\t            ;; Nowhere to land: the terminal event has none either.\n   252\t            (let [entry (claim! boundary xid)]\n   253\t              (swap! (:state boundary) update :awaiting dissoc xid)\n   254\t              (when entry (drop-socket! entry))\n   255\t              {:http/status :http/gone :http/exchange xid})\n   256\t            (let [[old _] (swap-vals! (:state boundary)\n   257\t                                      (fn [s]\n   258\t                                        (cond-> (update s :awaiting dissoc xid)\n   259\t                                          (contains? (:open s) xid)\n   260\t                                          (assoc-in [:open xid :requested?] true))))]\n   261\t              (when-let [event (get-in old [:awaiting xid])]\n   262\t                (deposit! boundary (terminal-event xid event)))\n   263\t              {:http/status :http/accepted :http/exchange xid})))))))\n   264\t\n   265\t\n   380\t(defn- race\n   381\t  \"Run every fn in `fs` on its own thread released together; wait for all.\"\n   382\t  [fs]\n   383\t  (let [start (java.util.concurrent.CountDownLatch. 1)\n   384\t        threads (mapv (fn [f]\n   385\t                        (doto (Thread. (fn [] (.await start) (f)))\n   386\t                          (.start)))\n   387\t                      fs)]\n   388\t    (.countDown start)\n   389\t    (doseq [^Thread t threads] (.join t 5000))))\n   390\t\n   391\t\n   392\t(deftest competing-closers-produce-exactly-one-terminal-event\n   393\t  (dotimes [_ 200]\n   394\t    (let [{:keys [b ingress]} (boundary)\n   395\t          [id trace] (open! b)\n   396\t          wins (atom 0)]\n   397\t      (race (repeat 4 #(when (http/close-exchange b id) (swap! wins inc))))\n   398\t      (is (= 1 @wins) \"exactly one competing claim owns the exchange\")\n   399\t      (is (= [:http/request :http/closed] (mapv :http/event (events ingress id))))\n   400\t      (is (= 1 (count (filter #{[:close]} @trace))) \"the socket is closed once\"))))\n   401\t\n   402\t\n   403\t(deftest a-terminal-during-the-request-deposit-lands-after-the-request\n   404\t  (testing \"deterministic: the peer closes while the request event is being deposited\"\n   405\t    (let [ring (medium 16)\n   406\t          b (atom nil)\n   407\t          id-seen (atom nil)\n   408\t          ingress (reify\n   409\t                    stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   410\t                    (append! [_ v]\n   411\t                      (when (and (= :http/request (:http/event v)) (nil? @id-seen))\n   412\t                        (reset! id-seen (:http/exchange v))\n   413\t                        (http/peer-closed! @b (:http/exchange v)))\n   414\t                      (stream/append! ring v)))\n   415\t          egress (medium 16)]\n   416\t      (reset! b (http/make-boundary\n   417\t                  {:ingress {:dao.stream/handle ingress :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   418\t                   :ingress-admission admission\n   419\t                   :egress {:dao.stream/handle egress :dao.stream/surface #{:reader}}\n   420\t                   :http/max-open 4 :http/max-body-bytes 16}))\n   421\t      (let [res (http/accept! @b (req) (scripted (atom [])))\n   422\t            id (:http/exchange res)]\n   423\t        (is (= :http/accepted (:http/status res)))\n   424\t        (is (= [:http/request :http/closed] (mapv :http/event (events ring id)))\n   425\t            \"request first, then exactly one terminal\")\n   426\t        (is (empty? (http/open-exchanges @b))))))\n   427\t  (testing \"stress: a closer races the accepting call\"\n   428\t    (dotimes [_ 200]\n   429\t      (let [{:keys [b ingress]} (boundary)\n   430\t            trace (atom [])\n   431\t            res (atom nil)\n   432\t            closer (fn []\n   433\t                     ;; the id is [incarnation n]; close whatever is open\n   434\t                     (doseq [id (http/open-exchanges b)] (http/close-exchange b id)))]\n   435\t        (race [#(reset! res (http/accept! b (req) (scripted trace))) closer closer])\n   436\t        (let [id (:http/exchange @res)\n   437\t              evs (mapv :http/event (events ingress id))]\n   438\t          (is (= :http/request (first evs)))\n   439\t          (is (<= (count (filter #{:http/closed} evs)) 1) \"never a duplicate terminal\")\n   440\t          (when (empty? (http/open-exchanges b))\n   441\t            (is (= [:http/request :http/closed] evs) \"a closed exchange has its terminal\")))))))\n     1\t(ns dao.star.signals\n     2\t  \"Decode a request's client signals from an `:http/request` event\n     3\t   (docs/design/dao.star.md, Signals).\n     4\t\n     5\t   Signals are the client's unverified claim, so `decode` is total: a missing,\n     6\t   malformed or non-map input answers `{}` and nothing throws.  GET and DELETE\n     7\t   carry them in the query parameter the spec names, every other method in the\n     8\t   JSON body.  The JSON parse is the host's; a host without one decodes\n     9\t   nothing.\n    10\t\n    11\t   Scope: the JSON and URL-decoding seams are implemented for the JVM and\n    12\t   ClojureScript only.  On ClojureDart they are unimplemented, and `decode`\n    13\t   throws `ex-info` naming the seam (`:dao.star.signals/seam`) rather than\n    14\t   answer `{}`, which would be indistinguishable from absent signals.\"\n    15\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n    16\t            [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n    17\t            [dao.host.text :as text]\n    18\t            #?(:clj [clojure.data.json :as json])))\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\t#_{:clj-kondo/ignore [:unused-private-var]}\n    22\t(defn- unimplemented\n    23\t  [seam]\n    24\t  (throw (ex-info (str \"dao.star.signals: no \" (name seam) \" seam on this host\")\n    25\t                  {:dao.star.signals/seam seam})))\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\t(defn- parse-json\n    29\t  [s]\n    30\t  #?(:cljd (unimplemented :json)\n    31\t     :clj (json/read-str s :key-fn keyword)\n    32\t     :cljs (js->clj (js/JSON.parse s) :keywordize-keys true)))\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t(defn- url-decode\n    36\t  [s]\n    37\t  #?(:cljd (unimplemented :url-decode)\n    38\t     :clj (java.net.URLDecoder/decode ^String s \"UTF-8\")\n    39\t     :cljs (js/decodeURIComponent (str/replace s \"+\" \" \"))))\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\t(defn- body-text\n    43\t  [body]\n    44\t  (cond (string? body) body\n    45\t        (bytes/bytes? body) (text/utf8-decode body)\n    46\t        :else nil))\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(defn- query-param\n    50\t  [query k]\n    51\t  (when (string? query)\n    52\t    (some (fn [pair]\n    53\t            (let [[name value] (str/split pair #\"=\" 2)]\n    54\t              (when (= k name) (or value \"\"))))\n    55\t          (str/split query #\"&\"))))\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\t(defn decode\n    59\t  \"The signals map of request `event`, or `{}`.\"\n    60\t  [event]\n    61\t  (try\n    62\t    (let [raw (if (contains? #{:get :delete} (:http/method event))\n    63\t                (some-> (query-param (:http/query event) \"datastar\") url-decode)\n    64\t                (body-text (:http/body event)))\n    65\t          parsed (when (and (string? raw) (not (empty? raw))) (parse-json raw))]\n    66\t      (if (map? parsed) parsed {}))\n    67\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n    68\t      (if (:dao.star.signals/seam (ex-data e))\n    69\t        (throw e)\n    70\t        {}))))\n    45\t\n    46\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    47\t;; Finding 5: stage until the grant is observed; fail closed\n    48\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    49\t\n    50\t(deftest the-begin-page-waits-for-the-lineage-grant-to-be-observed\n    51\t  (let [w (h/world)]\n    52\t    ;; the judges tick, the driver has no reading yet\n    53\t    (tick-only! w [:exchange :lineage] 10)\n    54\t    (let [x (h/call! w :get \"/\")]\n    55\t      (h/pump! w)\n    56\t      (is (= 1 (count (driver/sessions (:driver w)))) \"the root fact was appended\")\n    57\t      (is (empty? (h/effects w x)) \"no begin page before the grant is observed\")\n    58\t      (tick-only! w [:driver] 10)\n    59\t      (is (= [:http/head :http/chunk :http/end] (mapv :http/effect (h/effects w x)))\n    60\t          \"answered once the grant is observed\"))))\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\t(deftest an-input-waits-while-the-holder-has-no-reading\n    64\t  (let [w (h/start! (h/world))\n    65\t        s (h/begin-lineage! w)\n    66\t        w2 (h/world)]\n    67\t    (is (some? s))\n    68\t    (testing \"a session whose driver never ticks consumes nothing\"\n    69\t      (tick-only! w2 [:exchange :lineage] 10)\n    70\t      (let [x (h/call! w2 :get \"/\")]\n    71\t        (h/pump! w2)\n    72\t        (let [s2 (first (driver/sessions (:driver w2)))\n    73\t              y (h/call! w2 :post (str \"/k/\" s2) \"{}\")]\n    74\t          (h/pump! w2)\n    75\t          (is (empty? (h/effects w2 y)))\n    76\t          (is (empty? (filter #(= :consumption (facts/fact-kind %)) (h/values (:facts w2)))))\n    77\t          (is (empty? (h/effects w2 x))))))))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t(deftest a-subscription-projection-waits-for-its-exchange-grant\n    81\t  (let [w (h/start! (h/world))\n    82\t        s (h/begin-lineage! w)\n    83\t        sub (h/call! w :get (str \"/s/\" s))]\n    84\t    ;; router and driver only: the exchange judge has not granted yet\n    85\t    (router/router-step! (:router w))\n    86\t    (driver/driver-step! (:driver w))\n    87\t    (is (contains? (driver/subscriptions (:driver w) s) sub))\n    88\t    (is (empty? (h/effects w sub)) \"no head or projection before the grant\")\n    89\t    (h/pump! w)\n    90\t    (is (= [:http/head :http/chunk] (mapv :http/effect (h/effects w sub))))))\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    94\t;; Finding 6: pending publication respects the bound\n    95\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    96\t\n    97\t(defn- staged-world\n    98\t  \"A session with one input staged: the facts medium refused its fact.\"\n    99\t  []\n   100\t  (let [w (h/start! (h/world))\n   101\t        s (h/begin-lineage! w)\n   102\t        _ (reset! (:failing? w) true)\n   103\t        x (h/input! w s \"{\\\"inc\\\":1}\")]\n   104\t    (is (some? (get-in @(:driver w) [:sessions s :unpublished])) \"staged\")\n   105\t    [w s x]))\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\t(deftest a-staged-transition-is-dropped-past-the-bound\n   109\t  (let [[w s x] (staged-world)]\n   110\t    (reset! (:failing? w) false)\n   111\t    ;; only the driver's clock moves: its holder reaches the bound\n   112\t    (stream/append! (get-in w [:ticks :driver]) (dl/tick {:ms 200}))\n   113\t    (driver/driver-step! (:driver w))\n   114\t    (is (nil? (get-in @(:driver w) [:sessions s :unpublished])) \"dropped\")\n   115\t    (is (empty? (h/consumption-facts w)))\n   116\t    (is (empty? (h/effects w x)) \"the requester sees silence\")))\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\t(deftest a-staged-transition-is-dropped-after-the-lease-lapses\n   120\t  (let [[w s x] (staged-world)]\n   121\t    (reset! (:failing? w) false)\n   122\t    (let [lease-id (some #(when (= {:dao.star/lineage s} (:dao.lease/subject %))\n   123\t                            (:dao.lease/lease %))\n   124\t                         (h/values (:lineage-lease w)))]\n   125\t      (stream/append! (:lineage-lease w) (dl/lapsed lease-id :silence))\n   126\t      (driver/driver-step! (:driver w)))\n   127\t    (is (nil? (get-in @(:driver w) [:sessions s :unpublished])))\n   128\t    (is (empty? (h/consumption-facts w)))\n   129\t    (is (empty? (h/effects w x)))))\n   130\t\n   131\t\n   132\t(deftest a-staged-transition-waits-through-a-gap-and-never-publishes\n   133\t  (let [[w s x] (staged-world)]\n   134\t    (reset! (:failing? w) false)\n   135\t    (dotimes [_ 70] (stream/append! (:lineage-lease w) {:junk true}))\n   136\t    (driver/driver-step! (:driver w))\n   137\t    (is (lease/gapped? (agent-of w s)))\n   138\t    (h/pump! w)\n   139\t    (is (some? (get-in @(:driver w) [:sessions s :unpublished])) \"still staged\")\n   140\t    (is (empty? (h/consumption-facts w)) \"a gapped holder publishes nothing\")\n   141\t    (is (empty? (h/effects w x)))))\n   142\t\n   143\t\n   144\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   145\t;; Finding 7: consumption independent of emission\n   185\t\n   186\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   187\t;; Finding 8: a gap on every medium the driver reads\n   188\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   189\t\n   190\t(defn- subscribed\n   191\t  [opts]\n   192\t  (let [w (h/start! (h/world (merge {:duration-ms 1000} opts)))\n   193\t        s (h/begin-lineage! w)\n   194\t        sub (h/call! w :get (str \"/s/\" s))]\n   195\t    (h/pump! w)\n   196\t    (dotimes [_ 40] (h/advance! w 10))\n   197\t    [w s sub]))\n   198\t\n   199\t\n   200\t(defn- flood-ticks!\n   201\t  [w n]\n   202\t  (dotimes [_ n]\n   203\t    (let [now (swap! (:clock w) inc)]\n   204\t      (stream/append! (get-in w [:ticks :driver]) (dl/tick {:ms now})))))\n   205\t\n   206\t\n   207\t(deftest a-gap-on-any-medium-forgets-subscriptions-and-stops-renewals\n   208\t  (doseq [[medium opts trigger]\n   209\t          [[:tick {:driver-tick-capacity 8}\n   210\t            (fn [w _] (flood-ticks! w 20))]\n   211\t           [:lineage-lease {}\n   212\t            (fn [w _] (dotimes [_ 70] (stream/append! (:lineage-lease w) {:junk 1})))]\n   213\t           [:exchange-lease {}\n   214\t            (fn [w _] (dotimes [_ 70] (stream/append! (:exchange-lease w) {:junk 1})))]\n   215\t           [:view {:session-capacity 8}\n   216\t            (fn [w s]\n   217\t              (let [out (get-in @(:driver w) [:sessions s :vm-out])]\n   218\t                (dotimes [_ 20] (stream/append! out (assoc {} :count 0)))\n   219\t                (h/input! w s)))]\n   220\t           [:begin {}\n   221\t            (fn [w _] (dotimes [_ 40] (stream/append! (:begin w) {:junk 1})))]]]\n   222\t    (let [[w s sub] (subscribed opts)]\n   223\t      (is (pos? (renewals w)) (str medium \": renewing while healthy\"))\n   224\t      (is (contains? (driver/subscriptions (:driver w) s) sub))\n   225\t      (trigger w s)\n   226\t      (driver/driver-step! (:driver w))\n   227\t      (is (empty? (driver/subscriptions (:driver w) s)) (str medium \": subscriptions forgotten\"))\n   228\t      (let [before (renewals w)]\n   229\t        (dotimes [_ 10] (h/advance! w 10))\n   230\t        (is (= before (renewals w)) (str medium \": no renewal after the gap\"))))))\n   231\t\n   232\t\n   233\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   234\t;; Finding 9: a grant published before the holder's first tick is not lost\n   235\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   236\t\n   237\t(deftest a-grant-published-before-the-holders-first-tick-is-observed-later\n   238\t  (let [w (h/world)]\n   239\t    (tick-only! w [:exchange :lineage] 10)\n   240\t    (h/call! w :get \"/\")\n   241\t    (h/pump! w)\n   242\t    (let [s (first (driver/sessions (:driver w)))\n   243\t          agent (agent-of w s)]\n   244\t      (is (some #(= :dao.lease/accepted (:dao.lease/status %)) (h/values (:lineage-lease w)))\n   245\t          \"the judge has published the grant\")\n   246\t      (is (not (lease/granted? agent)) \"the holder has no reading yet\")\n   247\t      (tick-only! w [:driver] 10)\n   248\t      (is (lease/granted? agent) \"observed once a reading exists\"))))\n   249\t\n   250\t\n   251\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   252\t;; Finding 10: a failed release is retried\n   253\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   254\t\n   255\t(deftest a-failed-release-is-retried-on-later-passes\n   256\t  (let [w (h/start! (h/world {:program h/one-shot-program}))\n   257\t        s (h/begin-lineage! w)\n   258\t        agent (agent-of w s)\n   259\t        released? #(some (fn [f] (= :dao.lease/released (:dao.lease/status f)))\n   260\t                         (h/values (:facts w)))]\n   261\t    (reset! (:failing? w) #(= :dao.lease/released (:dao.lease/status %)))\n   262\t    (h/input! w s)\n   263\t    (is (some #(= (facts/ended s :halted) %) (h/values (:facts w))) \"the lineage ended\")\n   264\t    (is (not (released?)) \"the release append failed\")\n   265\t    (is (lease/release-pending? agent))\n   266\t    (reset! (:failing? w) false)\n   267\t    (h/pump! w)\n   268\t    (is (released?) \"retried and appended\")\n   269\t    (is (not (lease/release-pending? agent)))))\n   270\t\n   271\t\n   272\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   273\t;; Finding 11: tests that fail if the order is reversed\n   274\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   275\t\n   276\t(defn- hooked\n   277\t  \"A reader/writer over `handle` that runs `hook!` once, before serving its\n   278\t   first read.\"\n   279\t  [handle hook!]\n   280\t  (let [fired (atom false)]\n   281\t    (reify\n   282\t      stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   283\t      (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor handle))\n   284\t      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   285\t      (cursor [_ anchor] (stream/cursor handle anchor))\n   286\t      (next [_ cursor]\n   287\t        (when (compare-and-set! fired false true) (hook!))\n   288\t        (stream/next handle cursor))\n   289\t      stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   290\t      (append! [_ v] (stream/append! handle v)))))\n   291\t\n   292\t\n   293\t(deftest the-fact-is-published-and-its-request-deposited-inside-one-pass\n   294\t  (let [ingress (h/medium 16) facts-m (h/facts-log) lease-m (h/medium 16)\n   295\t        begin (h/medium 16) session (h/medium 16)\n   296\t        hooked-ingress (hooked ingress\n   297\t                               (fn []\n   298\t                                 ;; during the router's read of the ingress: the\n   299\t                                 ;; fact is accepted, then its request deposited\n   300\t                                 (stream/append! facts-m (facts/root \"s\"))\n   301\t                                 (stream/append! ingress\n   302\t                                                 {:http/exchange [1 1] :http/event :http/request\n   303\t                                                  :http/method :post :http/path \"/k/s\"})))\n   304\t        r (router/make-router {:ingress hooked-ingress :facts facts-m :lease lease-m\n   305\t                               :begin begin :co-located? true\n   306\t                               :facts-declaration (lease/facts-declaration)\n   307\t                               :session-medium (constantly session)})]\n   308\t    (router/router-step! r)\n   309\t    (is (empty? (h/values begin)) \"never begin\")\n   310\t    (is (= [:input] (mapv :kind (h/values session)))\n   311\t        \"ingress is read first, then the fact is drained, then the request classified\")))\n   312\t\n   313\t\n   314\t(deftest a-token-is-chased-with-single-passes\n   315\t  (let [w (h/start! (h/world {:duration-ms 1000000}))\n   316\t        s (h/begin-lineage! w)]\n   317\t    (loop [token s i 1]\n   318\t      (when (<= i 15)\n   319\t        (let [x (h/call! w :post (str \"/k/\" token) \"{\\\"inc\\\":1}\")\n   320\t              text (loop [n 0]\n   321\t                     (pass! w)\n   322\t                     (let [t (h/sse-text w x)]\n   323\t                       (if (or (str/includes? t \"data-occ\") (> n 20)) t (recur (inc n)))))]\n   324\t          (is (str/includes? text (str \">\" i \"<\")) (str \"input \" i \" consumed in single passes\"))\n   325\t          (recur (h/occ-of text) (inc i)))))))\n   326\t\n   327\t\n   328\t(deftest renewals-land-at-the-interval-and-under-half-the-duration\n   329\t  (let [w (h/start! (h/world {:duration-ms 100}))\n   330\t        s (h/begin-lineage! w)\n   331\t        _ (h/call! w :get (str \"/s/\" s))\n   332\t        _ (h/pump! w)\n   333\t        interval (get (:interval w) :ms)\n   334\t        marks (loop [i 0 last-count (renewals w) out []]\n   335\t                (if (= i 40)\n   336\t                  out\n   337\t                  (do (h/advance! w 10)\n   338\t                      (let [c (renewals w)]\n   339\t                        (recur (inc i) c (if (> c last-count) (conj out @(:clock w)) out))))))\n   340\t        gaps (map - (rest marks) marks)]\n   341\t    (is (>= (count marks) 3) \"renewing repeatedly\")\n   342\t    (is (= 30 interval) \"the interval is sized by lease/renewal-interval\")\n   343\t    (doseq [g gaps]\n   344\t      (is (>= g interval) \"never before the interval has elapsed\")\n   345\t      (is (< g 50) \"strictly under half the 100 ms duration\"))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The committed-state fixes resolve both terminal-event races, and the cap and complete-history changes match the revised ruling. Two holder-discipline gaps remain: patches are emitted before exchange holders observe that pass’s ticks or lapses, and an exchange-lease gap removes only the affected subscription. I’m checking the tests for those cases."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/dao/star/r3_test.clj; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/driver.cljc | sed -n '43,70p;126,144p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/router.cljc | sed -n '48,80p;112,140p'; rg -n 'subscription|max|Sizing|Keep-alive' docs/design/dao.star.md; sed -n '100,148p' test/dao/star/driver_test.clj; head -32 test/dao/star/r2_test.clj; nl -ba test/dao/star/loopback_test.clj | sed -n '136,150p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/dao/star/r3_test.clj; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/driver.cljc | sed -n '43,70p;126,144p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/router.cljc | sed -n '48,80p;112,140p'; rg -n 'subscription|max|Sizing|Keep-alive' docs/design/dao.star.md; sed -n '100,148p' test/dao/star/driver_test.clj; head -32 test/dao/star/r2_test.clj; nl -ba test/dao/star/loopback_test.clj | sed -n '136,150p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.star.r3-test\n     2\t  \"Round r3: the exchange lease's tenure cap (dead-peer bound on a host that\n     3\t   reports neither close nor failed write) and the complete-history\n     4\t   session-facts medium.\"\n     5\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n     6\t            [dao.star.driver :as driver]\n     7\t            [dao.star.driver-test :as h]\n     8\t            [dao.star.facts :as facts]\n     9\t            [dao.star.lease :as lease]\n    10\t            [dao.star.router :as router]\n    11\t            [dao.stream :as stream]))\n    12\t\n    13\t\n    14\t(defn- stream-append!\n    15\t  [w v]\n    16\t  (stream/append! (:facts w) v))\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\t(defn- refused\n    20\t  \"The :refused key of an assembly refusal, or :assembled.\"\n    21\t  [f]\n    22\t  (try (f) :assembled\n    23\t       (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e (:refused (ex-data e)))))\n    24\t\n    25\t\n    26\t(def ^:private evicting {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity 16 :value-domain :portable-values})\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\t(deftest constructors-refuse-a-facts-medium-that-is-not-complete-history\n    30\t  (let [w (h/world)\n    31\t        driver-config (:config @(:driver w))\n    32\t        xl-config {:ingress (:ingress w) :egress (:egress w) :lease-medium (:exchange-lease w)\n    33\t                   :tick (get-in w [:ticks :exchange]) :open-exchanges (constantly #{})\n    34\t                   :close-exchange (constantly true) :units h/units :duration {:ms 100}\n    35\t                   :cadence {:ms 10} :tolerance {:ms 0} :capacity 8\n    36\t                   :subscription-max {:ms 400}}\n    37\t        ll-config {:facts (:facts w) :lease-medium (:lineage-lease w)\n    38\t                   :tick (get-in w [:ticks :lineage]) :retire! identity :units h/units\n    39\t                   :duration {:ms 100} :cadence {:ms 10} :tolerance {:ms 0}\n    40\t                   :facts-declaration (lease/facts-declaration)}\n    41\t        router-config {:ingress (:ingress w) :facts (:facts w) :lease (:lineage-lease w)\n    42\t                       :begin (:begin w) :co-located? true\n    43\t                       :session-medium (constantly nil)\n    44\t                       :facts-declaration (lease/facts-declaration)}]\n    45\t    (testing \"the complete declaration assembles\"\n    46\t      (is (= :assembled (refused #(driver/make-driver driver-config))))\n    47\t      (is (= :assembled (refused #(lease/make-lineage-lease ll-config))))\n    48\t      (is (= :assembled (refused #(router/make-router router-config)))))\n    49\t    (testing \"an :evict-oldest declaration is refused on the declaration\"\n    50\t      (is (= :session-facts (refused #(driver/make-driver\n    51\t                                        (assoc driver-config :facts-declaration evicting)))))\n    52\t      (is (= :session-facts (refused #(lease/make-lineage-lease\n    53\t                                        (assoc ll-config :facts-declaration evicting)))))\n    54\t      (is (= :session-facts (refused #(router/make-router\n    55\t                                        (assoc router-config :facts-declaration evicting)))))\n    56\t      (is (= :session-facts (refused #(router/make-router (dissoc router-config :facts-declaration))))))\n    57\t    (testing \"a subscription cap is required\"\n    58\t      (is (= :assembled (refused #(lease/make-exchange-lease xl-config))))\n    59\t      (is (= :subscription-cap (refused #(lease/make-exchange-lease\n    60\t                                           (dissoc xl-config :subscription-max)))))\n    61\t      (is (= :subscription-cap (refused #(lease/make-exchange-lease\n    62\t                                           (assoc xl-config :subscription-max {:ms 0}))))))))\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\t(deftest session-facts-keep-the-root-past-any-ring-capacity\n    66\t  (let [w (h/start! (h/world))\n    67\t        s (h/begin-lineage! w)\n    68\t        old-ring-capacity 256]\n    69\t    (dotimes [i (* 2 old-ring-capacity)]\n    70\t      (stream-append! w (facts/ended (str \"other-\" i) :halted)))\n    71\t    (let [r (lease/drain (:facts w) (lease/oldest-cursor (:facts w)))]\n    72\t      (is (not (:gap? r)) \"a complete-history medium cannot gap\")\n    73\t      (is (> (count (:values r)) old-ring-capacity))\n    74\t      (is (= (facts/root s) (first (:values r))) \"the root is still readable from the origin\"))\n    75\t    (testing \"and the router still routes the old lineage as live\"\n    76\t      (h/pump! w)\n    77\t      (is (= :current (:kind (facts/resolve-token (router/index (:router w)) s)))))))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    81\t;; Ruling 3: the tenure cap bounds a subscription whose driver keeps renewing\n    82\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    83\t\n    84\t(defn- renewals\n    85\t  [w]\n    86\t  (count (filter #(= :dao.lease/renewal (:dao.lease/event %)) (h/values (:egress w)))))\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t(deftest a-subscription-the-driver-keeps-renewing-ends-at-its-cap\n    90\t  (let [w (h/start! (h/world {:duration-ms 100 :subscription-max-ms 200}))\n    91\t        s (h/begin-lineage! w)\n    92\t        sub (h/call! w :get (str \"/s/\" s))\n    93\t        quiet (h/call! w :get \"/unrouted\")\n    94\t        grant-of (fn [x] (some #(when (= {:http/exchange x} (:dao.lease/subject %)) %)\n    95\t                               (h/values (:exchange-lease w))))]\n    96\t    (h/pump! w)\n    97\t    (testing \"only the subscription's grant carries the cap\"\n    98\t      (is (= {:ms 200} (:dao.lease/max (grant-of sub))))\n    99\t      (is (nil? (:dao.lease/max (grant-of quiet)))))\n   100\t    (testing \"the driver renews on its ticks while the cap is not reached\"\n   101\t      (dotimes [_ 10] (h/advance! w 10))\n   102\t      (is (pos? (renewals w)))\n   103\t      (is (contains? @(:open w) sub))\n   104\t      (is (contains? (driver/subscriptions (:driver w) s) sub)))\n   105\t    (testing \"past the cap renewal stops, the reclaim closes it, and the lapse is recorded\"\n   106\t      (dotimes [_ 20] (h/advance! w 10))\n   107\t      (let [after (renewals w)]\n   108\t        (dotimes [_ 10] (h/advance! w 10))\n   109\t        (is (= after (renewals w)) \"no renewal after the bound\"))\n   110\t      (is (not (contains? (driver/subscriptions (:driver w) s) sub)) \"dropped by the driver\")\n   111\t      (is (not (contains? @(:open w) sub)) \"close-exchange ran\")\n   112\t      (is (some #(= {:http/exchange sub :http/event :http/closed} %) (h/values (:ingress w)))\n   113\t          \":http/closed was deposited\")\n   114\t      (is (some #(and (= :dao.lease/lapsed (:dao.lease/status %))\n   115\t                      (= (:dao.lease/lease (grant-of sub)) (:dao.lease/lease %))\n   116\t                      (= :cap (:dao.lease/cause %)))\n   117\t                (h/values (:exchange-lease w)))\n   118\t          \":lapsed was recorded with cause :cap\"))\n   119\t    (testing \"the never-answered exchange still lapses by silence\"\n   120\t      (is (not (contains? @(:open w) quiet)))\n   121\t      (is (some #(and (= (:dao.lease/lease (grant-of quiet)) (:dao.lease/lease %))\n   122\t                      (= :silence (:dao.lease/cause %)))\n   123\t                (h/values (:exchange-lease w)))))))\n    43\t(defn make-driver\n    44\t  \"Assemble the driver.  Config:\n    45\t     :facts :egress :begin     media handles (the session-facts writer, the\n    46\t                               egress writer, the begin handler's medium)\n    47\t     :tick                     the drivers' tick stream (handle)\n    48\t     :lineage-lease            the lineage-lease medium (handle, read for grants)\n    49\t     :exchange-lease           the exchange-lease medium (handle, read for grants)\n    50\t     :program                  a `dao.await` process reading `in`, writing `out`\n    51\t     :project-fn :begin-fn     the composition's projections\n    52\t     :units :lineage-renewal-interval :exchange-renewal-interval\n    53\t     :session-capacity         declared capacity of each session medium\n    54\t     :facts-declaration        the session-facts medium's declaration; refused\n    55\t                               (`:refused :session-facts`) unless\n    56\t                               `:retention :complete`\n    57\t     :lease-capacity           declared capacity of the lease media\"\n    58\t  [{:keys [program project-fn begin-fn] :as config}]\n    59\t  (when-not (and (map? program) (fn? project-fn) (fn? begin-fn))\n    60\t    (throw (ex-info \"the driver needs :program, :project-fn and :begin-fn\"\n    61\t                    {:refused :config})))\n    62\t  (lease/check-facts-declaration! (:facts-declaration config))\n    63\t  (atom {:config config\n    64\t         :begin-cursor (lease/oldest-cursor (:begin config))\n    65\t         :sessions {}}))\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\t(defn session-medium\n    69\t  \"The routed-input medium of lineage `s`, or nil: the router's forward target.\"\n    70\t  [driver s]\n   126\t  [x]\n   127\t  {:http/exchange x :http/effect :http/end})\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(defn- answer!\n   131\t  \"Head, one SSE projection, end: the reply to a one-shot exchange.\"\n   132\t  [config x occurrence model]\n   133\t  (emit! config [(head x \"text/event-stream\")\n   134\t                 (chunk-fx x ((:project-fn config) occurrence model))\n   135\t                 (end x)]))\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\t(defn- patch!\n   139\t  [config s]\n   140\t  (let [{:keys [occurrence model]} (:latest s)]\n   141\t    (doseq [x (keys (:subs s))\n   142\t            :when (not (contains? (:sub-staged s) x))]\n   143\t      (emit! config [(chunk-fx x ((:project-fn config) occurrence model))]))))\n   144\t\n    48\t(defn make-router\n    49\t  \"Assemble the router.  Config:\n    50\t     :ingress        the boundary's ingress medium (may be a reflection)\n    51\t     :facts          the session-facts medium, a direct handle\n    52\t     :lease          the lineage-lease medium, a direct handle\n    53\t     :begin          the begin handler's medium (handle)\n    54\t     :session-medium (fn [lineage] -> handle or nil)\n    55\t     :facts-declaration  the facts medium's declaration, `:retention :complete`\n    56\t   The facts and lease handles are classification media: a reflection answers\n    57\t   `blocked` while its request is pending, which says nothing about the source,\n    58\t   so the router refuses at assembly (ex-info `:refused :co-located`) unless\n    59\t   both are direct handles declared `:co-located? true`.\"\n    60\t  [{:keys [ingress facts lease begin session-medium co-located?] :as config}]\n    61\t  (lease/check-facts-declaration! (:facts-declaration config))\n    62\t  (when-not (and co-located?\n    63\t                 (not (reflection? facts))\n    64\t                 (not (reflection? lease)))\n    65\t    (throw (ex-info \"the router reads its classification media directly: declare :co-located? true with direct (non-reflection) handles\"\n    66\t                    {:refused :co-located})))\n    67\t  (when-not (and ingress facts lease begin (fn? session-medium))\n    68\t    (throw (ex-info \"the router needs :ingress :facts :lease :begin :session-medium\"\n    69\t                    {:refused :config :config (dissoc config :ingress :facts :lease :begin)})))\n    70\t  (atom {:config config\n    71\t         :ingress-cursor (lease/oldest-cursor ingress)\n    72\t         :facts-cursor (lease/oldest-cursor facts)\n    73\t         :lease-cursor (lease/oldest-cursor lease)\n    74\t         :index facts/empty-index\n    75\t         :routes {}\n    76\t         :gaps 0}))\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\t(defn index\n    80\t  [router]\n   112\t      nil)))\n   113\t\n   114\t\n   115\t(defn router-step!\n   116\t  \"One pass, in the spec's order.  Answers the router.\"\n   117\t  [router]\n   118\t  (let [s @router\n   119\t        {:keys [ingress facts lease]} (:config s)\n   120\t        in (lease/drain ingress (:ingress-cursor s))\n   121\t        fs (lease/drain facts (:facts-cursor s))\n   122\t        ls (lease/drain lease (:lease-cursor s))]\n   123\t    (swap! router\n   124\t           (fn [s]\n   125\t             (-> s\n   126\t                 (assoc :ingress-cursor (:cursor in)\n   127\t                        :facts-cursor (:cursor fs)\n   128\t                        :lease-cursor (:cursor ls))\n   129\t                 (update :gaps + (if (:gap? in) 1 0))\n   130\t                 (update :index #(reduce facts/index-step % (:values fs)))\n   131\t                 (update :index #(reduce facts/index-step % (:values ls))))))\n   132\t    (doseq [event (:values in)\n   133\t            :when (map? event)]\n   134\t      (route! router event))\n   135\t    router))\n35:5. **Effects Out**: The agent appends to the egress `dao.stream`, tagged with the exchange id: an `:http/head` effect (status, `Content-Type: text/event-stream`), one `:http/chunk` per SSE event with the fully constructed string, and `:http/end` when the response is complete. A subscription exchange simply never ends.\n82:**One input, one successor.** Consuming an input advances occurrence `O` to its successor `O'` and appends the lineage fact. The reply goes to the exchange that carried the consumed input; patches for the session go to its open subscription exchanges, which the driver holds as its own interpreter state, built from the subscribe requests and terminal events routed to it.\n92:**The open exchange is leased.** The judge runs inside the peer that holds the HTTP boundary and is composed with the boundary's `close-exchange` as reclaim procedure and `open-exchanges` as its inventory (`dao.stream.http.md`, Inventory). For each `:http/request` it observes it grants unsolicited on a lease medium it writes: subject `{:http/exchange x}`, holder the egress medium's identity, a duration in `{:ms 1 :s 1000}`, and a `:dao.lease/max` cap that subscription exchanges are required to carry, so no subscription is uncapped (architect ruling 2026-10-24, `collab/1792841840885-architect-dao-star-m1-reconcile-r2`). Reclaim closes the exchange; the adapter deposits `:http/closed`, then the judge records `:lapsed`. A responder that keeps an exchange open observes its grant and appends `{:dao.lease/event :dao.lease/renewal :dao.lease/lease L}` to the egress medium at under half the duration, from its own control flow, against its own tick stream. The judge and `egress-step` are peer observers of that medium; each ignores the other's facts. A one-shot responder answers inside the granted duration and renews nothing. An exchange nobody answers lapses by `:silence`; Datastar's reconnect opens a new one.\n94:**A gap is loss, and nothing is forwarded about it.** The judge, on an ingress `gap`, reconciles both ways against the inventory: an open exchange without a lease is granted afresh, and a leased exchange absent from the inventory is recorded `:lapsed` with cause `:policy`, so nothing is held unleased and nothing closed stays leased (inventory reconciliation; `dao.lease.md`'s reclaim-and-regrant is reserved for a lost ledger). The router forwards nothing about a gap: a request or terminal event lost in the evicted window is unrouted, and a forward whose `append!` answers anything but `ok` is the same loss; an unrouted request's exchange lapses by `:silence`. Drivers learn that an exchange is gone from the lease medium they already read for their grants: a `:lapsed` record for one of their exchanges drops it (`dao.lease.md`, Carriage). A driver whose cursor on any medium it reads answers `gap` forgets every subscription it holds and renews none; they lapse by `:silence` and close, and Datastar's reconnect subscribes again. Session media are declared at assembly like any deposit destination, evict-oldest with a capacity, and sized against the driver's lag.\n96:**Keep-alive is the responder's.** On its tick it may append an `:http/chunk` carrying an SSE comment line. That chunk is bytes for the wire, so a host that reports write failure discovers a dead peer by writing; the renewal is evidence for the judge. Neither stands in for the other. A peer's close or a reported write failure is deposited as `:http/closed`; the responder reads it as data and drops the exchange, and the judge ends the exchange lease with cause `:policy`. A host whose send buffers and whose close notification is silent for an idle exchange (http-kit is one) reports neither, so a chunk written to a dead peer is not evidence of anything, and a responder that keeps renewing a subscription it believes open keeps the lease alive. Such an exchange ends at its lease's `:dao.lease/max`, not before (architect ruling 2026-10-24, `collab/1792841840885-architect-dao-star-m1-reconcile-r2`).\n98:**The lineage is leased** (owner ruling 2026-10-07; the holder choice below is the architect's). A lineage nobody returns to is reclaimed through `dao.lease.md`, not by a timer. The peer holding the parked record is the grantor. When a lineage begins, its judge grants unsolicited on the lease medium: subject and holder `{:dao.star/lineage S}`, duration the composition's idle allowance, `:dao.lease/max` optional. Attribution is by envelope key: the session-facts medium is written only by session drivers, each stamping `:dao.star/lineage` on its facts, renewals and release, and the judge's resolver reads that key; until ShiBi, any writer of that medium can renew, the same exposure the exchange lease has. The driver observes its grant before consuming or projecting, renews at under half the duration from its own control flow, on each consumed input and on its tick while it holds an open subscription, and **stops at its bound**: past it, it consumes nothing and projects nothing, and an input arriving then is handed to the root program as begin. So a connected session is retained for as long as it stays connected, by design, bounded only by the cap; a disconnected one lapses after the idle allowance. The lease ends with the lineage: released by the driver on halt, lapsed by the judge on silence. Reclaim retires the runnable resource, the current parked record; the `:lapsed` record on the lease medium is the judge's own and is what ends the lineage for the router. History, successor facts and lease records are kept (`dao.lease.md`: a reclaim frees the resource, never the record). The subject is distinct from Mode 2's custody subject `{:yin.k/occurrence O}` on the arbitration medium. Leases are process-scoped until the composition settles the three durable duties `dao.lease.md` names.\n100:Sizing: duration exceeds twice the renewal interval; the keep-alive interval stays under the shortest proxy or NAT idle timeout on the path; the ingress window exceeds router and judge lag and each session medium's window exceeds its driver's; a boundary restart loses sockets and ledger together, so its exchange inventory to reclaim is empty. The duration bounds silence, not death. The detection bound for a peer that disconnects while an exchange is idle is the exchange lease's `:dao.lease/max` on a host that does not report the close, and the host's own close notification, when it gives one, on a host that does. The composition sizes `:dao.lease/max` against the longest it will tolerate a dead subscription holding a socket and a driver slot, and accepts that every healthy subscription reconnects at that interval. A false lapse is possible (`dao.lease.md`, Limits).\n152:- **No hidden state**: a driver's open subscriptions and the router's token index are interpreter state derived from media each reads with its own cursor, rebuilt from those media or honestly lost on a gap.\n156:- **Multi-shot forks** (Arc's back button resuming a sibling branch): branch identity and subscription routing with a non-unique current are unspecified.\n  ([{:keys [program ingress-capacity session-capacity retire? duration-ms subscription-max-ms\n          driver-tick-capacity]\n     :or {program counter-program ingress-capacity 64 session-capacity 64\n          retire? true duration-ms 100 subscription-max-ms 1000000\n          driver-tick-capacity 64}}]\n   (let [dur {:ms duration-ms}\n         interval (dl/renewal-interval units dur {:ms (quot (* 3 duration-ms) 10)}\n                                       {:ms (quot duration-ms 10)})\n         failing? (atom false)\n         ingress (medium ingress-capacity)\n         egress (medium 256)\n         raw-facts (facts-log)\n         facts-medium (gated raw-facts failing?)\n         lineage-lease (medium 64)\n         exchange-lease (medium 64)\n         begin (medium 32)\n         ticks {:driver (medium driver-tick-capacity) :exchange (medium 64) :lineage (medium 64)}\n         open (atom #{})\n         clock (atom 0)\n         drv (driver/make-driver\n               {:facts facts-medium :egress egress :begin begin\n                :tick (:driver ticks) :lineage-lease lineage-lease\n                :exchange-lease exchange-lease :program program\n                :project-fn project :begin-fn begin-page :units units\n                :lineage-renewal-interval interval\n                :exchange-renewal-interval interval\n                :session-capacity session-capacity :lease-capacity 256\n                :facts-declaration (lease/facts-declaration)})\n         close-exchange (fn [id]\n                          (when (contains? @open id)\n                            (swap! open disj id)\n                            (stream/append! ingress {:http/exchange id\n                                                     :http/event :http/closed})))\n         xl (lease/make-exchange-lease\n              {:ingress ingress :egress egress :lease-medium exchange-lease\n               :tick (:exchange ticks) :open-exchanges (fn [] @open)\n               :close-exchange close-exchange :units units :duration dur\n               :cadence {:ms 10} :tolerance {:ms 0} :capacity 256\n               :subscription-max {:ms subscription-max-ms}})\n         ll (lease/make-lineage-lease\n              {:facts raw-facts :lease-medium lineage-lease :tick (:lineage ticks)\n               :retire! (fn [s] (when retire? (driver/retire! drv s)))\n               :units units :duration dur :cadence {:ms 10} :tolerance {:ms 0}\n               :facts-declaration (lease/facts-declaration)})\n         rt (router/make-router\n              {:ingress ingress :facts raw-facts :lease lineage-lease :begin begin\n               :co-located? true :facts-declaration (lease/facts-declaration)\n               :session-medium (fn [s] (driver/session-medium drv s))})\n         w {:ingress ingress :egress egress :facts raw-facts :failing? failing?\n(ns dao.star.r2-test\n  \"Review round r2 for dao.star Mode 1: staging until grants are observed,\n   fail-closed tenure checks, consumption independent of emission, gap\n   handling on every medium, grants published before a holder's first tick,\n   failed-release retry, and the strengthened order and bound tests.\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.await :as await]\n            [dao.lease :as dl]\n            [dao.star.driver :as driver]\n            [dao.star.driver-test :as h]\n            [dao.star.facts :as facts]\n            [dao.star.lease :as lease]\n            [dao.star.router :as router]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]))\n\n\n(defn- tick-only!\n  \"Move only the named tick streams (keys of `(:ticks w)`) to `now` and pump.\"\n  [w ks now]\n  (doseq [k ks]\n    (stream/append! (get-in w [:ticks k]) (dl/tick {:ms now})))\n  (h/pump! w))\n\n\n(defn- pass!\n  \"Exactly one of every stepped part, no repetition.\"\n  [w]\n  (lease/exchange-lease-step! (:xl w))\n  (lease/lineage-lease-step! (:ll w))\n  (router/router-step! (:router w))\n  (driver/driver-step! (:driver w))\n   136\t            (recur))))))\n   137\t\n   138\t\n   139\t(deftest boundary-reclaim-ends-the-response-and-deposits-http-closed\n   140\t  ;; http-kit never reports a client-initiated close of an idle streaming\n   141\t  ;; exchange (reproduced without any dao code: no on-close after FIN or RST\n   142\t  ;; and further writes), so the socket here is closed from the boundary's side\n   143\t  ;; by the reclaim procedure, and the test asserts what the composition then\n   144\t  ;; observes: the client reads the end of the chunked response (the\n   145\t  ;; terminator, not a TCP EOF: http-kit keeps the connection alive), the ingress carries :http/closed for that\n   146\t  ;; exchange, and the driver reads it as data and drops the exchange.\n   147\t  (let [{:keys [port ingress boundary drv stop!]} (compose)]\n   148\t    (try\n   149\t      (let [page (roundtrip port \"GET\" \"/\" nil)\n   150\t            s (second (re-find #\"data-root=\\\"([^\\\"]+)\\\"\" page))]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'defn reading-ok\\\\?|defn duration\\\\?|defn observe-grant|reading-ok\\\\? holder reading' src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc; sed -n '1739,1786p' src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc; head -38 src/cljc/dao/star/lease.cljc; sed -n '20,35p' test/dao/star/driver_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'defn reading-ok\\\\?|defn duration\\\\?|defn observe-grant|reading-ok\\\\? holder reading' src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc; sed -n '1739,1786p' src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc; head -38 src/cljc/dao/star/lease.cljc; sed -n '20,35p' test/dao/star/driver_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"78:(defn duration?\n1739:(defn observe-grant\n1775:  (if (and (reading-ok? holder reading)\n1823:      (not (reading-ok? holder reading)) false\n1853:    (not (reading-ok? holder reading)) holder\n1878:           (reading-ok? holder reading)\n1925:                (reading-ok? holder reading)\n(defn observe-grant\n  \"H1: observe the grant before acting. The grant is held only when the\n  fact is a structurally valid `:accepted` naming this holder\n  (`:dao.lease/holder` = `:self`) whose author, by the composition's\n  resolver bound to the source the fact was read from, is the grantor --\n  the same attribution seam the judge resolves with -- and, when the\n  state carries a `:subject` or `:proposal` expectation (wired at\n  assembly by a holder that proposed), the grant's subject and answered\n  proposal match it; a grant answering no proposal matches no proposal\n  expectation. Anything else -- a forged or non-grantor `:accepted`, a\n  grant naming another holder or another lease's proposal, a\n  structurally defective fact, a refusal -- establishes nothing: the\n  holder is returned unchanged and `:grant` nil is the report \\\"no grant\n  observed\\\"; a holder with `:grant` nil holds nothing, and every\n  discipline below answers false.\n\n  `reading` is the newest reading drained from the holder's OWN tick\n  cursor at the moment of observation -- the tenure basis no renewal\n  moves, which the cap binds -- and no clock supplies it. A reading that\n  is not a well-shaped, in-table, in-bound duration observes nothing\n  (mirroring the judge's first-tick rule; see `reading-ok?`).\n\n  Sizing is checked where the interval and the GRANTED duration are known\n  together, because the grantor may grant shorter than the ask: an\n  undersized grant -- interval + interval not strictly below the granted\n  duration, equality included -- is still HELD, recorded `:undersized?`:\n  the holder holds what it was granted, the grantor's word, and may\n  release it, but every discipline function treats it as at the bound --\n  no renewal is due, no renewal advances anything, `holding?` is false.\n\n  The first observed grant is the one held: observation seeds the basis\n  once, and no later fact moves it (a fresh lease id is a different\n  lease; a holder holding several threads one state per lease). A\n  resolver that throws propagates the throw: attribution failure is loud,\n  and the control flow observing through a broken seam observes nothing.\"\n  [holder source fact reading]\n  (if (and (reading-ok? holder reading)\n           (lease-fact? fact)\n           (= :dao.lease/accepted (get fact status-key))\n           (not (defective? fact (:units holder)))\n           (= (:self holder) (get fact :dao.lease/holder))\n           (= (:grantor holder) ((:resolver holder) source fact))\n           (nil? (:grant holder))\n           (or (nil? (:subject holder))\n               (= (:subject holder) (get fact :dao.lease/subject)))\n           (or (nil? (:proposal holder))\n               (= (:proposal holder) (get fact :dao.lease/proposal))))\n    (assoc holder\n(ns dao.star.lease\n  \"The dao.lease compositions of dao.star Mode 1 (docs/design/dao.star.md,\n   Liveness): the stream-reading helper, the holder agent a driver threads per\n   lease, and the two grantor-side wrappers (exchange lease, lineage lease)\n   that author grants and drive the judge.\n\n   Nothing here reads a clock.  Time is the `:dao.lease/reading` data drained\n   from a tick stream the composition feeds, so every lapse is driven by\n   appending a tick.\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n            [dao.lease :as lease]\n            [dao.star.facts :as facts]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]))\n\n\n(defn- ok?\n  [r]\n  (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n\n\n(defn oldest-cursor\n  [handle]\n  (let [r (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-oldest)]\n    (when-not (ok? r)\n      (throw (ex-info \"cannot mint a cursor\" {:outcome r})))\n    (:dao.stream/cursor r)))\n\n\n(defn drain\n  \"Read `handle` from `cursor` to `blocked`, never waiting.  Answers\n   `{:cursor c :values [v...] :gap? bool :end? bool}`: a `gap` is noted and\n   reading continues from its recovery cursor, as the contract has it.\"\n  [handle cursor]\n  (loop [c cursor values [] gap? false]\n    (let [r (stream/next handle c)]\n      (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n        :dao.stream/ok (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj values (:dao.stream/value r)) gap?)\n        :dao.stream/gap (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) values true)\n  [capacity]\n  (:dao.stream/handle (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer\n                                     :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity capacity})))\n\n\n(defn facts-log\n  \"A complete-history session-facts medium.\"\n  []\n  (:dao.stream/handle (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/memory-log})))\n\n\n(defn values\n  [handle]\n  (:values (lease/drain handle (lease/oldest-cursor handle))))\n\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-24 12:56:10 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-24 19:56:10 +07\n\nStatic confirmation only. No files edited, staged, or committed; no suites rerun.\n\nPaths below are relative to the worktree.\n\n| Finding | Resolution | File:line evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Duplicate terminal events | **Resolved** | `src/cljc/dao/stream/http.cljc:148` derives ownership from the committed prior state. Competing claims cannot both obtain the entry. |\n| 2. Lost terminal event | **Resolved** | `http.cljc:133` and `:256` derive both sides of the handshake from committed transitions. Either accepting or finishing owns the terminal deposit. |\n| 3. Unsupported dead-peer bound | **Resolved under revised ruling** | `src/cljc/dao/star/lease.cljc:274`, `:306`, `:329`, `:332` require and apply subscription caps, including inventory-recovered exchanges. `test/dao/star/r3_test.clj:89` checks renewal, reclaim, terminal deposit, and `:cap` lapse. |\n| 4. Evicting session facts | **Resolved** | `lease.cljc:239`, `:245`, `:356`; `driver.cljc:62`; `router.cljc:61` enforce complete-history declarations without capacity. Tests use memory-log; `r3_test.clj:65` verifies retained origin history. |\n| 5. Acting before grant / fail-open | **Partially resolved** | `driver.cljc:248`, `:336`, `:371` correctly stage initial responses and gate input handling. Subsequent patches and staged subscription flushing still bypass required tenure checks; details below. |\n| 6. Pending publication bypasses bound | **Resolved** | `driver.cljc:279` drops pending work after bound/lapse; `:282` prevents publication while not holding. Tests cover bound, lapse, and gap. |\n| 7. Consumption depends on emission | **Resolved** | `driver.cljc:313` stages a transition independently of model emission and retains the previous model when needed. `r2_test.clj:163` exercises inputs between emissions. |\n| 8. Gap handling | **Partially resolved** | Tick gaps are now tracked at `lease.cljc:99`; lineage gaps call `forget!` at `driver.cljc:425`. But exchange-holder gaps remove only one subscription at `:412`, rather than forgetting every subscription. |\n| 9. Grant skipped before first tick | **Partially resolved** | `lease.cljc:100` preserves grants while the reading is nil. A non-nil **invalid** first reading still advances the fact cursor without observing the grant. |\n| 10. Failed release not retried | **Resolved** | `driver.cljc:427` drives pending releases on later passes; `r2_test.clj:255` verifies failed publication followed by recovery. |\n| 11. Test adequacy | **Resolved for the original order/renewal concerns** | `r2_test.clj:293` would fail with facts-before-ingress ordering. `:314` chases tokens through individual passes. `:328` checks renewal spacing against the half-duration bound. |\n| 12. CLJD silently decodes `{}` | **Resolved as an explicit support limitation** | `signals.cljc:11`, `:30`, `:37`, `:68` disclose missing seams and propagate their exceptions instead of silently discarding supplied signals. CLJD functionality remains unimplemented and unverified. |\n\nThree blocking implementation gaps remain:\n\n1. **HIGH | `src/cljc/dao/star/driver.cljc:138`, `:336`, `:428` | Projection paths do not consistently enforce tenure.**  \n   `publish!` and `read-messages!` can emit subscription patches before `tick-subscriptions!` observes that pass’s exchange ticks and lapses. `patch!` checks only whether a subscription is staged. Advance the driver’s tick to an exchange’s cap while its lineage remains live, then process an input: a patch is appended before the exchange holder notices its bound.\n\n   The newly introduced `flush-subscriptions!` also checks only the exchange holder. A subscription staged while the lineage was live can receive its first projection after the lineage reaches its bound, if its exchange grant arrives later.\n\n   **Correction:** observe exchange-holder state before any subscription projection, and require both lineage and exchange tenure at every projection path. Add independently scheduled holder/judge tests.\n\n2. **HIGH | `src/cljc/dao/star/driver.cljc:412` | Exchange-lease gaps still receive incomplete cleanup.**  \n   The code drops only the exchange whose holder observed a gap. Another subscription with a newer cursor can remain and continue renewing, including renewing the lineage. The new gap test uses one subscription, so it cannot distinguish this behavior from forgetting all subscriptions.\n\n   **Correction:** propagate an exchange-holder gap to session-wide `forget!` handling before further renewals. Test two subscriptions with differently positioned lease cursors.\n\n3. **MEDIUM | `src/cljc/dao/star/lease.cljc:100` | Invalid first readings can permanently discard grants.**  \n   The new guard distinguishes nil from non-nil, rather than unusable from usable readings. For example, `{:ms 0}` passes this guard; `observe-grant` rejects it, but the fact cursor advances. A subsequent valid tick cannot recover that grant.\n\n   **Correction:** retain grants until a valid, in-table reading can observe them, or retain pending grants explicitly. Add invalid-first-reading followed by valid-reading coverage.\n\nThe remaining architectural qualifications are acceptable:\n\n- **(a) Unreachable facts-gap handling:** harmless defensive code, provided it is not presented as recovery from a permitted complete-history gap.\n- **(b) Requests remain unread without a tick:** correct fail-closed behavior. Supplying and driving holder tick streams is a composition duty.\n- **(c) `:subscription-max` sizing:** a composition choice. A 200 ms cap with a 100 ms duration is valid. Actual reclaim follows a completed judge pass; cap sizing must allow for cadence and reclaim cost.\n- **Untested CLJD throw:** honest enough for explicitly scoped JVM delivery; it does not establish CLJD support. The opening “total / nothing throws” docstring should be qualified to match the later scope exception. Green CLJD tests that never require these namespaces provide no additional assurance.\n\nThe renamed loopback test now accurately describes boundary reclaim and the chunked-response terminator. It does not claim real client-disconnect detection.\n\n**NOT SIGNED OFF**"}}
